hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18037","(18037) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hujar, on the authority of Tawus, who said: Sunnah divorce is when a man divorces. His wife is pure without intercourse, then he leaves her until her waiting period is over."
"18038","(18038) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khaled al-Hadha’i, on the authority of Abu Qalabab; He used to say regarding divorce of the Sunnah: He should divorce her one time, then leave her until she finds out about her."
"18039","(18039) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Yahya ibn Atiq, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Ali said: If people were to the point of divorce, no man would regret having a wife. He divorces her once, then leaves her until she has menstruated three times. menstruation"
"18040","(18040) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They would have liked for him to divorce her. One time, then he leaves her until she has had three menstrual periods."
"18041","(18041) Shabab bin Siwar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad; Regarding divorce in the Sunnah, they said: A man divorces his wife, then leaves her until her waiting period is over."
"18042","(18042) Abu Amer Al-Aqdi told us, on the authority of Abdul-Hakim bin Abi Farwa, who said: I heard Omar bin Abdul-Aziz He said: What is the matter with men when one of them says to his wife: Go to your family, and he divorces her to her family, but he refrained from doing so. That is the most severe of the prohibitions. Abdul-Hakim said: What he means by that is the waiting period."
"18043","(18043) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Jabir was asked about a pregnant woman: How can she be divorced? He said: He will divorce her once, then leave her until she gives birth."
"18044","(18044) Abu Bakr al-Hanafi told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, who said: Did I ask about that az-Zuhri? He said: There is a time for all of this."
"18045","(18045) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad, who said: If she is pregnant, he can divorce her whenever he wants."
"18046","(18046) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, who said: It was desirable for a pregnant woman to divorce a single woman, then leave her. Until you are humbled"
"18047","(18047) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Amir, who said: A pregnant woman may be divorced by her family."
"18048","(18048) Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: If a man divorces his wife while she is menstruating So do not rely on it. Al-Zuhri and his followers said the same."
"18049","(18049) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah Ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; Concerning the one who divorces his wife while she is menstruating, he said: Do not observe that menstruating woman."
"18050","(18050) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: If a man divorces his woman while she is menstruating, She did not observe that menstrual period."
"18051","(18051) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: If a man divorces his wife while she is menstruating, she does not observe the waiting period for that woman. Menstruation"
"18052","(18052) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Do not take it seriously."
"18053","(18053) Abbad bin Al-Awwam and Abd bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab said: Do not take it seriously."
"18054","(18054) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Do not take it seriously."
"18055","(18055) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: If he divorces her while she is menstruating, she does not observe the waiting period for that woman. Menstruation"
"18056","(18056) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who divorces his wife after she has menstruated, he said: She should not be observed."
"18057","(18057) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Malik bin Dinar, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, who said: No. She must observe that menstrual period."
"18058","(18058) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id and Khalas, who said: Do not observe that woman. Menstruation"
"18059","(18059) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid Ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Do not take her seriously."
"18060","(18060) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: It was recited from Read it"
"18061","(18061) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He used to say: She should observe that menstrual period."
"18062","(18062) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Anas bin Sirin, who said: I said to Ibn Umar: Did you count on her? He said: He said: His mouth, which means divorce."
"18063","(18063) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Yunus bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn age; He divorced his wife while she was menstruating, and it was said to him: Did you seek reward from her? Meaning divorce, he said: So he said: What prevents me if I am unable and have become foolish?"
"18064","(18064) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: If he wanted The man may divorce her three times due to the Sunnah. He divorced her once after each period of purification, and she should observe the waiting period for another menstrual period. Her divorce"
"18065","(18065) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: She has another menstrual period after her last divorce."
"18066","(18066) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Qalab; He hated to divorce his wife at every menstrual period, but he did that to prolong her life. So if he does that, then her waiting period is from the beginning as long as he does not take it back."
"18067","(18067) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to say: If a man divorces his wife and she remains for a month, then he divorces her another time, then her waiting period from the beginning Divorce unless he reconsiders it."
"18068","(18068) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab; Regarding a man who divorces his wife twice at the time of her menstruation, he said: She must observe the waiting period from the first divorce, as long as she did not renew it."
"18069","(18069) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Khaythamiyah; They both said: Whenever she menstruates, she is divorced, and she must wait for another menstrual period after the third. Waki` said: And the people are against him."
"18070","(18070) Abu Dawud al-Talisi told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, and Khalas bin Amr, They both said: She should observe the waiting period following her last divorce. Saeed bin Al-Musayyab said: We do not like that."
"18071","(18071) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He bore witness to Safiyya's return when he went back to her."
"18072","(18072) Muhammad bin Fudail told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; He was asked about a man who divorced his wife and then took her back, but he was unable to bear witness? He said: He bears witness when he knows."
"18073","(18073) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Amer; Concerning a man who divorces his wife and then has intercourse with her before witnessing that she has taken her back. He said: How can you say, O jealous woman? Concerning a man who did something to his wife without having any right to do so?"
"18074","(18074) Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Khaled Al-Nayli, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who divorced his wife and he testified, then he took her back and did not testify. He said: He was not forced to do so as a sin, but He was afraid that he would deny it."
"18075","(18075) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who divorces his wife and then cheats on her and does not testify. He said: His cheating has a recurrence, so let him testify."
"18076","(18076) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Shu’abi (h) and on the authority of Suleiman. Al-Taymi, on the authority of Tawus, they said: Intercourse is a recurrence, let him bear witness."
"18077","(18077) Yahya bin Abdul-Malik bin Abi Ghani told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak; In his saying: {And bear witness to those of justice among you} He said: They were commanded to bear witness at the time of divorce and reconciliation."
"18078","(18078) Ibn Abi Ghani told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hikam; Concerning a man who takes his wife and does not bear witness, he said: Let him bear witness that she has returned."
"18079","(18079) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Disunity and return are based on witnesses."
"18080","(18080) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hikam; Concerning a man who divorced his wife, then he vowed to commit adultery with her during her waiting period, and he learned of that after the waiting period had expired. He said: His cheating has its return."
"18081","(18081) Gandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham; Like that"
"18082","(18082) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn; He was asked about a man who was divorced and did not bear witness, and he came back and did not bear witness? He said: He divorced in a period other than the number of days, and took it back in a period other than the age, so that he could bear witness to what he had done."
"18083","(18083) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders; Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote: It is one and the same. This is the saying of his leaders."
"18084","(18085) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’atha’i, who said: If he returns In itself, it is nothing."
"18085","(18085) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Saeed, who said: He was asked about a man who said to his wife: If you enter so-and-so’s house, you are divorced. So she entered while he was not aware, until months had passed? So he told us on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, Saeed, and Khalas. They said: If he knew, he would bear witness to its review."
"18086","(18086) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who said: If you enter so-and-so’s house, you will divorce one woman, and you enter while he does not realize it. He said: If he had an affair with her, The number is broken and there is no reversal, otherwise it has disappeared from it with just one."
"18087","(18087) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Waqi’ bin Sahban, who said: Imran bin Husayn was asked about a man who divorced His wife three times in a meeting? He said: He has sinned against his Lord, and his wife has been forbidden to him."
"18088","(18088) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Malik ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: A man came to him and said: My uncle He divorced his wife three times and said: Your uncle disobeyed God, so God regretted him and did not make a way out for him."
"18089","(18089) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Shaqiq bin Abi Abdullah, on the authority of Anas, who said: Whenever Omar brought a man, he divorced him. He hit his wife three times while they were sitting, beat him, and separated them."
"18090","(18090) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, who said: I said to Al-Qasim bin Muhammad: The man wants to He divorces his wife three times? He said: He divorces her in different places."
"18091","(18091) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Ibn Umar said: Whoever divorces his wife three times has disobeyed. His Lord, and his wife made clear to him."
"18092","(18092) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; Concerning a man who divorces his wife three times, he said: If he does so, he has disobeyed his Lord, and his wife has abandoned him."
"18093","(18093) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: They used to punish anyone who divorced three times while sitting. One"
"18094","(18094) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, who said: Muhammad was asked about a man who divorces his wife three times in one sitting? He said: I don't know of anything wrong with that. Abd al-Rahman bin Awf divorced his wife three times, so he did not find fault with that."
"18095","(18095) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: He did not see any harm in that."
"18096","(18096) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Safar, on the authority of Shu’bi; Concerning a man who wanted his wife to divorce her, he said: He should divorce her three times."
"18097","(18097) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: A man came to him and said: : You divorced your wife ninety-nine times? He said: What did they tell you? He said: They said: It has been forbidden to you. He said: Then Abdullah said: They wanted to spare you. She withdrew from you with three and left them alone. Aggression"
"18098","(18098) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah; He was asked about a man who divorced his wife a hundred times? He said: It is forbidden for three and ninety-seven transgressions."
"18099","(18099) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, and Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, who said: A man came to Abdullah, and he said: Did you divorce your wife a hundred times? He said: She has committed three sins from you, and the rest of them disobeyed you."
"18100","(18100) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahhab; There was an idle man in Medina who divorced his wife a thousand times, so he was brought to Omar and said: I was only playing, so Omar hung his head with a pearl. And he separated them."
"18101","(18101) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib, who said: A man came to Ali and said: Have you divorced your wife for a thousand? He said: She married three of you, and divide the rest of them among your wives."
"18102","(18102) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Harun bin Antar, on the authority of his father, who said: I was sitting with Ibn Abbas. Then a man came to him and said: O Ibn Abbas, he divorced his wife a hundred times, but I only said it once, so you can find out who he is. With three, is it one? He said: She made three of your burdens, and you bear the burden of ninety-seven."
"18103","(18103) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Amr ibn Murra narrated to me, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, he said: A man came to Ibn Abbas, and he said: You have divorced your wife a thousand or a hundred. He said: She has withdrawn from you for three, and the rest of them are burdened. She took verses May God bless you"
"18104","(18104) Waki’ and Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Abi Tahiyya, who said: A man came to Uthman and said: You have divorced your wife a hundred times. He said: Three make her unlawful to you, and ninety-seven are transgressions."
"18105","(18105) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim; He heard him narrating on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah; He was asked about a man who divorced his wife for a hundred days? He said: We made three prohibitions for him, and ninety-seven virtues."
"18106","(18106) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, he said: Sa’id al-Maqbari narrated to us, he said: A man came to Abdullah bin Omar and I were with him, so he said: O Abu Abdul Rahman, has he divorced his wife a hundred times? He said: She missed you by three, and ninety-seven, and God will judge you for them on the Day of Resurrection."
"18107","(18107) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Shurayh: He said: Did I divorce her a hundred times? He said: She has done three things for you, and the rest of them are extravagance and disobedience."
"18108","(18108) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Fadl ibn Dulham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A man came to Al-Hasan and said: I have divorced his wife. Alif said: The old woman has become tired of you."
"18109","(18109) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of a man from the people of Mecca, who said: A man came to Ali. He said: I divorced my wife a thousand times? He said: You shall prohibit the three for yourself, and divide the rest of them among your family."
"18110","(18110) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Alqamiya, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: A man came to him. He said: There was talk between me and my wife, so I divorced her as many times as there were times. He said: Did you speak of divorce? He said: Yes, he said: Abdullah said: God has made divorce clear, so whoever accepts it, it has been made clear to him, and whoever confuses himself, We will make it clear. By God, do not confuse yourselves and we will bear it for you. It is as you say. It is as you say."
"18111","(18111) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: If he had said it to the women of the worlds after To make them king, they were forbidden to him."
"18112","(18112) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Amr; Ibn Abbas was asked about a man who divorced his wife according to the number of stars? He said: The head of the Gemini is sufficient for that."
"18113","(18113) Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad al-Ammi told us, on the authority of Aamir al-Ahwal, on the authority of Amr ibn Shuaib, on the authority of his father, On the authority of his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no divorce except after marriage. (Tirmidhi 1181. Ahmad 2/207)"
"18114","(18114) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of someone who heard a peacock say: He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: There is no divorce except after marriage, and no emancipation before ownership. (Abdul Razzaq 11455)"
"18115","(18115) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Misra, on the authority of An-Nazzal, on the authority of Ali, he said: No. Divorce except after marriage. (Abu Dawud 2865; Abd al-Razzaq 1145)"
"18116","(18116) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: There is no divorce except after marriage. There is no emancipation except after his rule."
"18117","(18117) Hammad bin Khaled told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: There is no divorce. Except after marriage. Al-Zuhri said: If the marriage takes place, the divorce also takes place. (Hakim 419)"
"18118","(18118) Waki’ told us, he said: Hassan bin Saleh told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I don't care if I married her, or put my hand on this sari, meaning that it is lawful."
"18119","(18119) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir, He raised him; He said: No divorce before marriage. (Bayhaqi 319)"
"18120","(18120) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr; Did Marwan ask Ibn Abbas about us? He said: No divorce before marriage, and no emancipation before possession."
"18121","(18121) Abd ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab; Concerning a man who said: The day I marry so-and-so, he will be divorced. He said: It is nothing."
"18122","(18122) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, he said: I asked Mansour about a man to whom a woman was mentioned, and he said: The day I marry her. So is he divorced? He said: Al-Hasan did not consider it a divorce."
"18123","(18123) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Because he saw no harm in marrying the woman who said: The day I marry her, she will be divorced."
"18124","(18124) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, and Tawoos; Like him"
"18125","(18125) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdul Malik bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; Concerning a man who says: The day I marry so-and-so, he will be divorced. He said: It is nothing, but divorce after marriage."
"18126","(18126) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ma’rif bin Wasil, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit; Ali bin Hussein said: There is no divorce before marriage."
"18127","(18127) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein; He said: There is no divorce except after marriage."
"18128","(18128) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, who said: Abdullah bin Rifa’i Al-Ansari informed me that It was mentioned to Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab that a man from the Ansar was told: It was reported to us that you are proposing to so-and-so, a woman, their highness. The Ansari said: He is divorced if he marries her, so Abdullah claimed that he asked Saeed? He said: As for me, I do not see anything in it. Yahya said: And I heard that Urwah used to say about that the same as what Sa`id said."
"18129","(18129) Abu Asama and Waki’ told us, saying: Shu’abi told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of slice; He said: There is no divorce except after marriage."
"18130","(18130) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ma’rif, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Tawus; He said: There is no divorce before marriage. He said: And I asked Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman? He said: It is nothing."
"18131","(18131) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ma’rif bin Wasil, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Rawah Al-Dhabi, who said: I asked Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, And Mujahid, and generous, on the authority of a man who said: The day I marry so-and-so, he will be divorced? They said: It is nothing. He said: And Saeed said: Will there be a torrent before rain?"
"18132","(18132) Qubaisa narrated to us, saying: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Adam, Khalid’s client, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, he said: Ibn Abbas said: God Almighty said: {O you who have believed, when you marry believing women and then divorce them from before you touch them}, so there is no divorce unless there is marriage. (Saeed bin Mansour 1028)"
"18133","(18133) Ja’far bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Asama, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b and Nafi’ bin Jubayr, who said: There is no divorce except after marriage."
"18134","(18134) Abdullah bin Numayr and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, who said: There were Salim, Qasim, and Omar. Bin Abdul Aziz; They see it as permissible for him."
"18135","(18135) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: He should refrain from it."
"18136","(18136) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi (H), and on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: So When it happened"
"18137","(18137) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; He was asked about a man who said to his wife: Every woman I marry over you is divorced. He said: Every woman He marries her to Ali, so she is divorced."
"18138","(18138) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Marzuq, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If The man stipulated for the woman at the time of the marriage contract that every woman he marries to her is divorced, and every woman is secret. It is easy for her to be free, it is permissible for her."
"18139","(18139) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, who said: Al-Zuhri said: If the marriage takes place, the divorce also takes place."
"18140","(18140) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad; Concerning a man who said to his wife: Every woman I marry to you is divorced. He said: This is a time when he will come back to you."
"18141","(18141) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hanzala, who said: Al-Qasim and Salem were asked about a man who said: The day I marry so-and-so, he will be divorced? They said: It is as he said."
"18142","(18142) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Omar, who said: I asked Al-Qasim about a man who said: The day I get married So-and-so is divorced? He said: He is divorced. Omar was asked about a man who said: The day I marry so-and-so, he will owe me as much as my mother’s back. He said: He will not marry her until she commits blasphemy."
"18143","(18143) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qays, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad; He appointed a woman to marry her, so he asked Ibn Masoud? He said: Inform her of the divorce and then marry her."
"18144","(18144) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Omar bin Hamza; He asked Salim, Al-Qasim, Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman, Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Hazm, and Abdullah bin Abdul The Most Gracious, on the authority of a man who said: The day I marry so-and-so, he will be divorced forever? So they all said: He will not marry her."
"18145","(18145) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Shurayh; That a man asked him about a man who said: The day I marry so-and-so, he will be divorced? Shurayh said: If she hears about Wadi al-Nuka’, he is permissible for him, meaning she is divorced."
"18146","(18146) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Suwayd bin Najih Al-Kindi, who said: I asked Al-Sha’abi about a man who said: I married so-and-so and he is divorced, or today I will marry so-and-so and he is divorced? Al-Sha’bi said: It is as he said, so I said: Ikrimah claims that divorce occurs after marriage, so he said: Jarmuz is the client of Ibn Abbas."
"18147","(18147) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of his predecessors, he said: I said to Salim Ibn Abdullah: A man who said: Every woman. He marries her and she is divorced, and every female slave he buys is free, so he said: As for me, if I had not been married, I would not have married her. And I was not pleased."
"18148","(18148) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi (H) and on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, they said: When he said Everything is nothing."
"18149","(18149) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, and Makhoul; Concerning a man who says: Every woman I marry is divorced, because they were making that obligatory for him."
"18150","(18150) Abu Asama told us, he said: Abdul Malik bin Abi Suleiman told us, he said: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr about the man. He says: Every woman I marry is divorced? He said: How do you divorce what you do not own? Divorce is only after marriage."
"18151","(18151) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas and Ibn Masoud, who said: Concerning a man who divorced his wife. Three: Before he has intercourse with her, she is not permissible for him until she marries another husband."
"18152","(18152) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, who said: If a virgin divorces a single woman, he has They divorced her once and for all, and if he divorced her three times, she is not lawful for him until she marries another husband."
"18153","(18153) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Bukair bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Ata bin Yassar said: I was sitting with Abdullah bin Amr, and a man asked him about a man who divorced his wife as a virgin three times? Ata’ said: So I said: Three in the firstborn and one, and Abdullah bin Amr said: How do you know? You are only a storyteller and not a mufti. You declare one of them and you prohibit the three until you marry another husband."
"18154","(18154) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Bukair bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of a man from Al-Ansar is called: Muawiyah. Ibn Abbas, Abu Hurairah, and Aisha said: She is not permissible for him until she marries another husband."
"18155","(18155) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abu Sa’id; About the one who divorces his wife three times before consummating the sexual intercourse with her, and says: She is not lawful for him until she marries another husband."
"18156","(18156) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I heard Umm Salama being asked about A man who divorced his wife three times before he had intercourse with her? She said: She is not permissible for him unless someone else has intercourse with her."
"18157","(18157) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: If he divorced her three times before He enters it with it, so it is based on the status of the one entered with it."
"18158","(18158) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah; In the same way"
"18159","(18159) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ubaid Allah ibn Umar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar (h) and on the authority of Muhammad ibn Iyas. Ibn Bukayr, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, Ibn Abbas, and Aisha; Concerning a man who divorces his wife three times before he has intercourse with her, they said: It is not permissible for him until she marries another husband."
"18160","(18160) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Maqil; Concerning a man who divorces his wife three times before he has intercourse with her, he said: She is not lawful for him until she marries another husband."
"18161","(18161) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who marries a woman and divorces her three times before consummating the sexual intercourse with her. He said: If he says he has divorced three times, then speak to him. She is not lawful for him until she marries another husband, and if he divorces her three consecutive divorces, then that is also the case."
"18162","(18162) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he divorced her three times before consummating the sexual intercourse with her It is not permissible for her to marry another husband."
"18163","(18163) Abdah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; Regarding a man who divorces his wife three times before he has intercourse with her, he said: It is not permissible for him until she marries another husband."
"18164","(18164) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: She is not permissible for him until she marries another husband."
"18165","(18165) Hatim bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhul; Whoever divorces his wife before he has intercourse with her, she is not lawful for him until she marries another husband."
"18166","(18166) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Shaqiq bin Abi Abdullah, on the authority of Anas, who said: She is not permissible for him until she marries a husband. Change it"
"18167","(18167) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab, and Sa’id bin Jubayr, And Hamid bin Abdul Rahman, they said: She is not permissible for him until she marries another husband."
"18168","(18168) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Amer; Concerning a man who divorced his wife three times before consummating the sexual intercourse with her, he said: He forced him to do so."
"18169","(18169) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abd al-Ala, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaidah (h) and on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, they said: If he divorces her three times before consummating the sexual intercourse with her, she is not permissible for him until she marries a husband. Change it"
"18170","(18170) Ibn Ayyash told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Hikam; Concerning a man saying to his wife: You are divorced, you are divorced, you are divorced. He said: She is divorced with the first and the last two, it is nothing He said: I said: Who says this? He said: Ali, Zaid, and others, meaning before he entered with her."
"18171","(18171) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When he said to his wife Before he consummated it, you are divorced, you are divorced, you are divorced, so it became clear with one and two omitted."
"18172","(18172) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Fuqaimi, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If he said before If he enters with it, “You are divorced,” “You are divorced,” “You are divorced,” “it is void” with the first, and the other two, it is nothing."
"18173","(18173) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Khalas, he said: It was clear from the beginning."
"18174","(18174) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, who said: It is clear with the first, and two things are not of anything."
"18175","(18175) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: When he said to her, “You He is divorced, you are divorced, you are divorced, before he consummated the marriage with her, she was forbidden to him."
"18176","(18176) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: If he divorced her three times before He consummated the marriage with her, she is not lawful for him until she marries another husband, and if he says it is a secret, then she is permitted to marry another husband."
"18177","(18177) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos and Ata, that they said: If a man divorces his wife Three times before he entered into her, so it was one."
"18178","(18178) Affan bin Muslim told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, he said: Ayoub told us; Tawus said: Abu Al-Sahba’i came to Ibn Abbas and said to him: Bring some of your good deeds. Indeed, the three were counted upon. During the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr, Omar issued one principality, so when he saw the age of the people, they had followed each other in Divorce, so he allowed her to do so. (Muslim 1099. Abu Dawud 2192)"
"18179","(18179) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Tawoos, Ata, and Jabir bin Zaid; They said: If he divorces her three times before consummating the sexual intercourse with her, then he divorces her once."
"18180","(18180) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who divorced his wife once, then a man met him and said: Did you divorce your wife? He said: Yes, then another man met him and said: Did you divorce him? He said: Yes, then he said: If it was the first intention, then it is one."
"18181","(18181) A partner told us about a man who divorces a woman and the man meets him and says: Did you divorce him? He says: Yes, then another one meets him and says: Did you divorce him? So he says: Yes, so he told us on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ibn Maqil, and Al-Shu’bi. They said: If he wants the former, there is no problem."
"18182","(18182) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who divorced his wife and he met her, and it was said to him: Did you divorce your wife? He said: Yes, then it was said to him: Did you divorce your wife? He said: Yes, then that was brought to Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, and he said: He did not intend."
"18183","(18183) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Abd Rabbuh, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, who said: I asked him about a man who divorced He divorced his wife, then he divorced another woman, and there were two of them. Then a man met him and said: Did you divorce your wife? He said: Yes, he said: So he said: If he only wanted a divorce, then there is nothing wrong with him."
"18184","(18184) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Hammad; Concerning a man who said to his wife: You are divorced, and she said: What do you say? He said: You are absolutely divorced. Hammad said: If he wants to understand her, then there is no problem."
"18185","(18185) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a man who says to his wife: You are divorced. Are you divorced? Are you divorced? They said: It is three, except that it was the intention of the first one, and if he said, “Immediately repeat,” then it is like that."
"18186","(18186) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Uqba ibn Abi Al-Aizar, who said: I asked Abraham about a man who divorced his wife. One divorce, or two divorces. Then a man asked him: Did you divorce your wife such-and-such, three times, or four times? The man said: Yes? Ibrahim said: She was clear of it."
"18187","(18187) Abd bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who says to his wife: You are divorced for a period of years. He said: He will have intercourse with her on that day."
"18188","(18188) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; He did not postpone divorce."
"18189","(18189) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He did not postpone divorce."
"18190","(18190) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If he is divorced for a specified period of time, then"
"18191","(18191) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Furat, on the authority of Abd al-Karim, who said: Al-Zuhri used to say: You should observe the waiting period on the day of He said"
"18192","(18192) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Whoever sets a period of time regarding divorce, and that time enters, it falls. Divorce"
"18193","(18193) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Ubaid, on the authority of Makhoul; He used to say: Until the appointed time comes."
"18194","(18194) Muammar bin Sulaiman Al-Raqqi told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Bishr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: For his sake."
"18195","(18195) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr, who said: Jabir bin Zayd was asked about a man who said to his wife: : If I divorce such-and-such a month, will my wife be divorced until the beginning of the year? He said: I think that she is divorced until the specified term, and she is permissible for him for anything other than that."
"18196","(18196) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of Salma bin Nabata, on the authority of Abu Dharr; He said to a boy of his: He is old enough to be one year old."
"18197","(18197) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who said to his wife: “Immediately committed.” He said: “Talaqiqa” if he meant divorce."
"18198","(18198) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abd Rabbuh, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, who said: This is a divorce."
"18199","(18199) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Perform the waiting period with a single woman."
"18200","(18200) Abdul bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: It is one, and it is more deserving. With it"
"18201","(18201) Waki` told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, he said: I asked al-Hakam, and Hammad about a man who said to his wife: You are divorced. Divorced, are you divorced? What is the first intention? They said: It is one, and similarly, when he says: “Ididah”, then Ididah."
"18202","(18202) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, who said: If a man says to his wife: “Continue the waiting period.” He completed the waiting period and said: I intended one, so it was one."
"18203","(18203) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer; Concerning a man who said to his wife: “Iddah,” he intended three days. He said: “One.”"
"18204","(18204) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan; And this is the saying of his leaders, that they said: If a man says to his wife: “You will observe the waiting period three times,” it is not permissible for him until she marries him as a husband. Change it"
"18205","(18205) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer; Like him"
"18206","(18206) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, and Abu Hurri, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who says to his wife: You are divorced and observes the waiting period. He said: She is one. And if he says: You are divorced and observes the waiting period, then it is Two"
"18207","(18207) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He said: It is not permissible to divorce an insane person."
"18208","(18208) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: It is not permissible to divorce a person who is insane."
"18209","(18209) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Aban bin Uthman, on the authority of Uthman, who said: It is not There is no divorce for either an insane person or a drunkard."
"18210","(18210) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Harun, he said: I asked Ibn Sirin about the divorce of an insane person? He said: It is nothing, and the ruler will look into it and ask between the two parties that he is divorced and his right hand should be patient."
"18211","(18211) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr, who said: Jabir was asked about a man who divorced his wife and he Crazy, when his madness took him? He said: It is not permissible."
"18212","(18212) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: It is not permissible to divorce an insane person if he is found guilty of it. It is permissible."
"18213","(18213) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abis bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Ali, who said: Every divorce It is permissible, except for the divorce of the imbecile."
"18214","(18214) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abis bin Rabi’, who said: I heard Ali saying."
"18215","(18215) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Ali said: Every divorce is permissible, except divorce. The imbecile"
"18216","(18216) Abu Bakr al-Hanafi told us, on the authority of Asama, on the authority of Nafi’; Al-Mujbir ibn Abd al-Rahman divorced his wife, and he was an imbecile, so Ibn Umar ordered her to observe the waiting period, and it was said to him: He is an imbecile. He said: I did not hear God make an exception for someone who is absolutely immoral, or anything else."
"18217","(18217) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: There is no divorce for an imbecile, nor for a child."
"18218","(18218) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he divorces a man with an immoral mind when he recovers, permissible"
"18219","(18219) Abdou bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: His divorce is not With something"
"18220","(18220) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: It is not permissible to divorce him."
"18221","(18221) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: It is not permissible to divorce him."
"18222","(18222) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: There is no divorce."
"18223","(18223) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It used to be said: All divorces are permissible. Except for the divorce of the imbecile."
"18224","(18224) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: There is no divorce for an insane person."
"18225","(18225) Ali bin Musahir told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab; Concerning his death, he said: If he divorces her when he takes her, then there is nothing wrong with him, and if he regains consciousness, his divorce is permissible."
"18226","(18226) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; Like him"
"18227","(18227) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Hasan; If he is afflicted with the danger of insanity, he should be divorced. Al-Hasan said: He is not bound to him, and his leaders said: If he buys and sells, he is bound to him. If he is divorced in a state of insanity, he is not obligated to do so."
"18228","(18228) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; Concerning the calamity that befalls him now, he said: Divorcing him and emancipating him is permissible."
"18229","(18229) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Mu’tamir, on the authority of his followers, who said: Insanity is two insanities, and if he does not recover, he will not recover. It is permissible for him to divorce him, and if he is recovering, then he should be divorced if he recovers if he is obligated to do so."
"18230","(18230) Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, he said: We found in The book of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of Amr: If an insane person tampers with his wife, he will divorce his guardian."
"18231","(18231) Al-Dahhak ibn Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The guardian of the possessed person should be divorced, and let him wait. May he wake up."
"18232","(18232) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: Divorce of a man with a demented person. A person who has lost his mind is nothing, his divorce is to his guardian."
"18233","(18233) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, who said: I wrote to Abu Qulabab about a woman who had been married off to her. Insane, with no hope of recovery, divorced by his guardian? So he wrote to me: No, she is a woman whom God has tested with calamity, so let her be patient."
"18234","(18234) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: It is not permissible for him to divorce his guardian."
"18235","(18235) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: I wrote to Omar about A madman was afraid that he would kill his wife, so he wrote to me to postpone him for a year so that he could seek medical treatment."
"18236","(18236) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ghayath, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: It is not permissible to divorce a boy."
"18237","(18237) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: It is not permissible to divorce a boy."
"18238","(18238) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: If the boy becomes sensible Praying and fasting, his divorce is permissible. He said: Al-Hasan said: It is not permissible to divorce him until he reaches puberty."
"18239","(18239) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ismail bin Imran al-Anzi, who said: I was divorced while I was a boy who had not yet Do I have a wet dream? So I asked Saeed bin Al-Musayyab? He said: If you memorize the prayer and fast during Ramadan, your divorce is permissible."
"18240","(18240) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ali bin Malik, who said: I asked Al-Sha’bi about a boy who was divorced three times? He said: I do not think that, when he understood, the three seemed to be combined."
"18241","(18241) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of someone who heard Ali say: Conceal the marriage of boys."
"18242","(18242) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ali; Like a comprehensive hadith."
"18243","(18243) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: Complete the marriage between boys, and he said: Every divorce is permissible. Except for the divorce of the person with the final agreement and the immoral person."
"18244","(18244) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: It is not permissible to free a child, or marry him, or Something about something."
"18245","(18245) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’, he said: I asked Ibrahim about the divorce of a boy? He said: There are many women."
"18246","(18246) Waki’ narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning the divorce of a boy, he said: It is nothing, and there are many women."
"18247","(18247) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to give you and them in marriage. They are young, and they keep their marriage secret for fear that divorce will take place on their tongues. Sufyan said: When it happened, nothing was seen of it."
"18248","(18248) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Mus’ab, on the authority of Shuabi; Concerning the boy’s divorce: It is nothing."
"18249","(18249) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about the divorce of a boy? They said: It is not permissible."
"18250","(18250) Ismail bin Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, he said: A man from the people of the Levant narrated to me, whom I did not see any harm in, he said: We were on a campaign, and a friend of ours came and divorced his wife three times. When he recovered, they said to him: You said such-and-such. He said: What? Tell me, I said: A little of this, not a lot, and I do not know it. So a man from us rode to Omar bin Abdul Aziz in A pilgrim, and when he fulfilled his need, he asked him about that, and he paid tribute to him."
"18251","(18251) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Maymun bin Mihran, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz; Similar to the hadith of Ibn Aliyah, on the authority of Yunus."
"18252","(18252) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: He used to say: The divorce of the one who has been conclusive and the one who is feverish. He is a fool, and marrying an insane person is nothing."
"18253","(18253) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: It is not permissible to divorce the one who has decided, and the one who has lost power. His mind during his illness."
"18254","(18254) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr bin Haram, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid; Concerning the divorce of the finalized person who is foolish and has no reason, what does he say? He said: There is no divorce for him, and there is no emancipation for him as long as he continues like that."
"18255","(18255) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir (H) and Sharik, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, they said: A mutual divorce is not permissible."
"18256","(18256) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A mutual divorce is not permissible. Or someone to whom calamity has befallen in a manner other than tidings."
"18257","(18257) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Ayyub, who said: I wrote to Abu Qalabi asking him about a divorce. Al-Mubasim? So he wrote to me: As far as the witnesses testified about him, if he is of sound mind, then his divorce is permissible, and if he is not of sound mind, then his divorce is not. It is permissible"
"18258","(18258) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Divorcing a drunk person is permissible."
"18259","(18259) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He said: An-Nashwan divorce is permissible."
"18260","(18260) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’; He did not permit the divorce of a drunkard."
"18261","(18261) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad, that they said: His divorce is permissible, but it is painful. His back"
"18262","(18262) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad; They said: His divorce is permissible."
"18263","(18263) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab, who said: Divorcing a drunkard is permissible."
"18264","(18264) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Anbasa; Omar bin Abdul Aziz permitted the divorce of a drunkard and flogging him."
"18265","(18265) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, who said: He divorced a neighbor of mine who was drunk, so he ordered me to ask Saeed bin Al-Musayyab? He said: If the truth is corrected in him, separate him from his wife, and multiply eighty."
"18266","(18266) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: His divorce is permissible."
"18267","(18267) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Maimun, who said: It is permissible to divorce him."
"18268","(18268) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Hamid bin Abdul Rahman, who said: Divorce is permissible The drunkard"
"18269","(18269) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, saying: I told Malik: I narrated that Suleiman bin Yassar and Saeed bin Al-Musayyab said: Is your divorce permissible? He said: Yes."
"18270","(18270) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Al-Kharit, on the authority of Abu Labid; Omar permitted the divorce of a drunkard with the testimony of his wives."
"18271","(18271) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If he is divorced or emancipated, it is permissible for him, and he is established. May the punishment be upon him."
"18272","(18272) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: It is permissible to divorce him, and the punishment in His back"
"18273","(18273) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: Whoever is divorced while intoxicated by God, it is not a divorce. With anything, and whoever is divorced by Satan in intoxication, his divorce is permissible."
"18274","(18274) Amr bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Al-Haytham, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: The divorce of a drunkard permissible"
"18275","(18275) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Aban bin Uthman, on the authority of Uthman, who said: It was not It permits the divorce of a drunkard and an insane person. He said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz used to allow his divorce, and it hurt his back, until Aban told him about that."
"18276","(18276) Muhammad bin Sawa’i narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir bin Zayd, Ikrimah, Ata’, and Tawoos. They said: It is not permissible."
"18277","(18277) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed; Al-Qasim and Omar bin Abdul-Aziz did not permit the divorce of a drunk."
"18278","(18278) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabah, on the authority of Ata’; He was not able to reward it."
"18279","(18279) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hanzala, or someone else, on the authority of Tawus; It was not permissible for him."
"18280","(18280) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Sumait Al-Sadusi, who said: I proposed to a woman, and they said to me: We will not marry you. Until you divorce your wife three times. I said: I have divorced her three times. He said: So they married me off. Then they looked, and behold, my wife was with me. They said: Haven't you divorced your wife? I said: Yes, she was married to so-and-so, the daughter of so-and-so, so I divorced her. As for this woman, I did not divorce her, so she went to Shaqiq ibn Majza bin Thawr and he wanted to go to Othman, so I said: Ask the Commander of the Faithful about this, so he asked him? He said: His intention."
"18281","(18281) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; That a man was sitting with his wife on a pillow, and the man was satisfied, so he said to his wife: You are divorced, meaning the pillow. Tawoos said: I don't see anything wrong with you."
"18282","(18282) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He said: Divorce is what is meant by divorce."
"18283","(18283) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who says to his wife: I have freed you. He said: It is not a divorce, unless he intends to do so."
"18284","(18284) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ismail ibn Raja’, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Masruq said: Divorce is what he means. With divorce"
"18285","(18285) Bishr ibn Mufaddal narrated to us, on the authority of Siwar, who said: Abu Thamam narrated to us, and his wife is from our family; Kinanah ibn Naqab had a wife with him, and she bore him children in pre-Islamic times, so he said to her: What is above? Your scope is free, so I disputed with him to Al-Ash’ari, and he said: By what you said, did you mean divorce? He said: Yes, he said: We inherited it from you."
"18286","(18286) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who said to his wife: You are freed. He said: She divorced him, and he has more right to her."
"18287","(18287) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Muslim al-Hanafi, on the authority of Issa ibn Hattan, on the authority of al-Rayyan ibn Sabră Hanafi; He was sitting in the mosque of his people, so he took a vowel, and said: A divorced vowel, a divorced vowel, three times, and he said: So it was raised. To Ali, he said: What did you intend? He said: I made an intention with my wife. He said: So he separated them."
"18288","(18288) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdul Malik bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Ata’, he said: Ibn Masoud came. Concerning a man who said to his wife: Your pregnancy is upon your foreigners. So Ibn Masoud wrote to Omar, and Omar wrote: Let him meet me. With the harvest, so he brought him the harvest, so he sent for Ali, and Ali said to him: I adjure you by God, what did you intend? He said: My wife. He said: So he separated them."
"18289","(18289) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who said to his wife: I have given you permission, so marry me. He said: If he does not intend divorce, then it is nothing. He mentioned that to Al-Shaabi. Al-Sha’bi said: By the one who swears by him, it is easier than this to be a divorce."
"18290","(18290) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Abu Hurr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who said to his wife: Get out of my house. What makes you stay in my house? I do not have a wife. He said that three times. Al-Hasan said: This is one time. And he will see what he intended."
"18291","(18291) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who says to his wife: “I have no need of you.” He said: “His intention.”"
"18292","(18292) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Ubaid, on the authority of Makhoul; Concerning a man who said to his wife: I have no need of you. An alcoholic said: Nothing."
"18293","(18293) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sha’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam, and Hammad about a man who said to his wife: Go wherever you want. I have no need of you? They said: If he intends to divorce her, then divorce him with one, and he has more right to her."
"18294","(18294) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who said to his wife: Go out, cover yourself, go away, I have no need of you, so he will divorce you, if he intends Divorce"
"18295","(18295) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Ikrimah; Concerning a man who said to his wife: “Go back to your family.” He said: “This is one thing.” And his leaders said: “I do not consider this to be anything.”"
"18296","(18296) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Saleh, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Hakam; Concerning a man who said to his wife: “I have set you on your way.” He said: “His intention.” He said: “What do you think if he intended three times?” He said: “I fear that That will be it."
"18297","(18297) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Fudail, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If he says: No As I have the right to do, it is an irrevocable divorce."
"18298","(18298) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer; Like him"
"18299","(18299) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir (h) and on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibn Iqal, on the authority of Mus’ab ibn Sa’d, Abu Malik, and Abdullah ibn Shaddad, who said: If a man divorces his wife three times While she is pregnant, it is not permissible for her to marry another husband."
"18300","(18300) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the divorce was written in his hand, it is obligatory for him."
"18301","(18301) Ismail Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali Ibn Al-Hakam Al-Bunani, who said: A man narrated to me that a man had written a letter of divorce. His wife was on a pillow, so he was asked about that popular man, and he saw it as a divorce."
"18302","(18302) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; He was asked about a man who wrote about divorcing his wife and then regretted it, so he kept the letter? He said: If he withholds it, it is nothing, but if he keeps it, it is a divorce."
"18303","(18303) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who writes to his wife about divorcing her, and then appears to him to hold the letter. He said: It is nothing unless He speaks, and if he sends it to her, she will wait for it from the day the Scripture comes to her."
"18304","(18304) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abd al-Khaliq, on the authority of Hammad, who said: If a man writes to his wife: If he has intercourse with you This book of mine means you are divorced. If the letter did not come to her, then she is not divorced. If it was written: As for after, then you are divorced. He is divorced, so he is divorced, and Ibn Shubramah said: He is divorced."
"18305","(18305) Hushaym bin Bashir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and on the authority of Muhammad bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi (h) and on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a female slave, if she is divorced and has not yet reached menstruation, they say: She must wait for the months, but if she menstruates before the months have passed, She resumed her waiting period with menstruation, so if she menstruated after the months had passed, her waiting period has expired."
"18306","(18306) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who marries a slave girl and divorces her before she reaches menstruation. He said: She is waiting for three months. She menstruated before completing the three months, the number of months ended, and the number of menstruation resumed."
"18307","(18307) Zayd ibn Harun told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr, who said: Jabir ibn Zayd was asked about a female slave who was divorced. After her husband had intercourse with her, and she was not menstruating, so she observed the waiting period for two months and twenty-five nights, then she menstruated? He said: After that, she should wait for three recitations, and so said Ibn Abbas."
"18308","(18308) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a man has a woman, she has given up on her. The menstruating woman, or the slave girl who has not menstruated, so whenever he wants, he can divorce her."
"18309","(18309) Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, he said: It was strange for him to divorce the woman who had not menstruated at the time of the new moon."
"18310","(18310) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, he said: He divorces her when Welcome"
"18311","(18311) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the woman has stopped after menstruation, And the slave girl did not menstruate, so the man wanted to divorce him, so he divorced at the beginning of the crescent moon, and he did not divorce anyone else until the end of the moon. I counted it"
"18312","(18312) Ibn al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Hammad, who said: I asked him about a man who said: His wife is divorced, and he has four children. Did they forget? He said: He puts his hand on those verses he wishes. Muammar said: Al-Hasan used to say that."
"18313","(18313) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hamid, on the authority of Abu Ja’far; Indeed, Ali drew lots between them."
"18314","(18314) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers (h) and on the authority of a man, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, they said: If he named it something So that is what he named, and if he did not name any of them, then the divorce is valid for them."
"18315","(18315) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Saeed; That a leader of Banu Saad asked Al-Hasan, and the Sultan had appointed him as his successor? He said: You do as you intended."
"18316","(18316) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Omar bin Amir, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who said: He has divorced his wife three times, and he has wives, and he said: If he intended any of them, then he is the one he intended, and if If he did not intend any of them, let him choose whichever of them he wishes. And so are the family and the zahirah."
"18317","(18317) Ruh bin Ubadah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman al-Adni, who said: Abu Ja`far was asked about a man who had four Women, then one of them came out and said: You are absolutely divorced. So he entered upon them and found each one of them saying: This one, and this one says: Why didn’t he recognize her? Abu Ja`far said: All of it is from him."
"18318","(18318) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Shurayh said: If he begins with divorce and emancipation before the dual Divorce and emancipation took place, whether he swore or not. Saeed bin Jubayr said: If he does not break his oath, then it is not his fault."
"18319","(18319) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan (h) and Ismail bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If he submits the divorce Or he delays it, it is the same if he connects it with his words."
"18320","(18320) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab and Al-Hasan, who said: He has Whether he advances the divorce, or delays it."
"18321","(18321) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; Concerning the exception regarding divorce and emancipation, he said: He has two options, whether he advances the divorce or delays it."
"18322","(18322) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: If he initiates divorce, it takes place, and he breaks his oath, Or did he not break his oath? And Abraham used to say: And he does not know who is a partner."
"18323","(18323) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed Al-Zubaidi, he said: I came to my wife, and she said to me: You did not come. On this hour, unless you have a woman other than me, so I said: Every woman has been divorced three times besides you, so I asked Ibrahim? He said: It is nothing."
"18324","(18324) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim; He saw the exception in divorce."
"18325","(18325) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, Mujahid, and Al-Nakha’i, And Al-Zuhari, they said: If a man says to his wife: You are divorced, if I do not do such-and-such, God willing, then it is for him. His two"
"18326","(18326) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Haytham, on the authority of Hammad; Concerning a man who said to his wife: You are divorced, God willing. He said: He has a wife, and the ruling said something like that."
"18327","(18327) Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of his leaders, and Iyas bin Muawiyah; Concerning a man who said to his wife: He is divorced, God willing. They said: She has gone away from him."
"18328","(18328) Abdul bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: When he said to his wife: He is divorced, God willing, so he is divorced, and there is no exception to him."
"18329","(18329) Ismail bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Muadh bin Rifa’i, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: If a man says to his wife: You are divorced, God willing, then she is not divorced, and if he says to his servant: You are He is free, God willing, so he is free. (Daraqutni 94. Bayhaqi 361)"
"18330","(18330) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Talha al-Khuza’i, on the authority of Abu Yazid al-Madani, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: There is no divorce for the one who is forced or the persecuted."
"18331","(18331) Zaid bin Harun and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ali; He did not see forced divorce as anything."
"18332","(18332) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He abolished it."
"18333","(18333) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Thabit, the client of the people of Medina, on the authority of Ibn Umar and Ibn al-Zubayr, He said: They did not view forced divorce as anything."
"18334","(18334) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab; He did not see anything."
"18335","(18335) Yahya bin Bashir told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Rafi’, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: There is no divorce or emancipation. Ali is under duress."
"18336","(18336) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mansour, and Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He did not see forced divorce as anything."
"18337","(18337) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; He did not see anything. Abdul-Malik said in his hadith: Ata’ said: Polytheism is greater than divorce."
"18338","(18338) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, who said: I asked Ata’ about divorce under duress? He said: It is nothing."
"18339","(18339) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: He did not consider forced divorce and emancipation permissible."
"18340","(18340) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, God He overlooked three things for you: mistakes, forgetfulness, and what you were forced to do. (Abdul Razzaq 11416. Saeed bin Mansour 1145)"
"18341","(18341) Abu Asama told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman; One of the workers beat a man until he divorced his wife. He said: So he wrote about it to Omar bin Abdul Aziz. He said: He did not This is permissible."
"18342","(18342) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Salih, on the authority of Safiyya bint Shaybah, on the authority of Aisha, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no divorce or emancipation in a closed state.\n(Abu Dawud 2187. Ahmad 6/276)"
"18343","(18343) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Sayyar, who said: I said to Al-Sha’bi: They claim that you do not see divorce under duress as anything? He said: They are lying to me."
"18344","(18344) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Divorce under duress is permissible."
"18345","(18345) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is permissible, but it is something that he ransomed for. Himself"
"18346","(18346) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salma, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; He used to permit forced divorce."
"18347","(18347) Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of a man, whom he named, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: Forced divorce permissible"
"18348","(18348) Hussein bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaba; Forced divorce is permissible."
"18349","(18349) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the sword were placed on its sides, Then he divorced, I would have permitted his divorce."
"18350","(18350) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Concerning a man who is forced to do something like emancipation or divorce. He said: If the ruler forces him, it is permissible, and if the thieves force him It is not permissible."
"18351","(18351) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who had two wives. He forbade one of them from going out, but the one he had not forbidden went out, so he thought it was the one he had forbidden. To go out, and he said: So-and-so did you go out? You are divorced. He said: You will be divorced as he wanted and intended."
"18352","(18352) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: You may divorce all of them, you may divorce the one he wanted. By naming her, and this is divorced by saying to her: You are divorced."
"18353","(18353) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; He said about a man who said to his wife: If she goes out, then you are divorced. So a woman borrowed her clothes and put them on, and he saw her. He married her when she left the door, and he said: Did you do that? You are divorced. He said: His divorce is due to his wife."
"18354","(18354) Omar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I heard him say: If a man swears by his wife that she will not She went out, and another woman of his came out, and it was said to him: This is your wife, so he thought the other woman was her, so he divorced her. Ata’ said: Nothing."
"18355","(18355) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’, on the authority of his followers; Concerning a man who had two wives, and one of them came out. He said: Who is this? It was said: So-and-so, he said: She is divorced, and she was the one who was not named, he said: The divorce has taken place on all of them."
"18356","(18356) A partner told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer; Concerning a man who had two wives, or two slave girls, and he called one of them and said: You are divorced, and the other answered him, saying: The one he named is divorced, and if he says to his servant, then it is like that."
"18357","(18357) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who said to his wife: “Join your family.” He said: “His intention.”"
"18358","(18358) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir; Concerning a man who says to his wife: Go back to your family. He said: Nothing, unless he intends to divorce her in anger."
"18359","(18359) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: When he said: Al-Haqqi By your family, he said: This is one thing, and his leaders said: I do not consider this to be anything."
"18360","(18360) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam, and Hammad about a man who said to his wife: Go out, join your family, does he intend to divorce? They said: She is one, and he is more deserving of her return."
"18361","(18361) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Harith Al-Ukli; Concerning a man who has four wives, and he said to them: There have been three divorces between them. He said: She has divorced each one of them for three times. Divorces, and a man divorces half a divorce. He said: It is a complete divorce."
"18362","(18362) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who had four wives, and he said to them: There is a divorce between you. He said: There is a divorce for each woman."
"18363","(18363) Abu Asim Rawad bin Jarrah told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: It was said to Omar bin Abdul-Aziz: A man divorces Is his wife half divorced? He said: This is a divorce."
"18364","(18364) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hammad and his followers; Concerning a man who had four wives, and he said to them: There is a divorce between you. He said: It is upon each one of them. Divorce"
"18365","(18365) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If he says: You are divorced, half or a third A divorce means a divorce."
"18366","(18366) Ali ibn Mushir and Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Zurara ibn Awfa, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God has overlooked what your nation has narrated. themselves, unless they speak of it or act upon it. (Bukhari 2528, Muslim 202)"
"18367","(18367) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn Sirin and Al-Hasan, that they They said: Self-talk about divorce is nothing, and Ibn Sirin said: If he had not been asked, he would have been more beloved to me."
"18368","(18368) Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Ismail bin Adam, he said: I asked Muhammad bin Sirin about the man talking to himself about divorce? He said: Self-talk is nothing."
"18369","(18369) Hafs told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; Like him"
"18370","(18370) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd (h) and on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, they said: It is nothing."
"18371","(18371) Omar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’ (H) and on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid; In the same way"
"18372","(18372) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: If he spoke to himself of divorce or emancipation, It is nothing."
"18373","(18373) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man makes the affairs of his wife In the hand of someone else, so whatever he divorces is a single and final divorce."
"18374","(18374) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Joseph, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who puts his wife’s affairs in the hands of a man. He said: It is as he said."
"18375","(18375) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man saying to another man: Go and divorce so-and-so. He said: It is permissible, if he divorces him, it is permissible."
"18376","(18376) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, who said: Amer was asked about a man who put his wife’s affairs in the hands of another man. So the man divorced her three times? He said: She is one. He only made a matter of hers in his hand one time."
"18377","(18377) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad, who said: If a man places the affairs of his wife in the hands of a man, and he divorces, then One clear one."
"18378","(18378) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, who said: I heard Muammar mentioning on the authority of al-Zuhri; Concerning a man who authorizes the divorce of his wife by her own hand, or by the hand of her brother, or her father, or by the hand of anyone, so the word is what he said. If he divorces her one, then one, if he divorces her two, then two, and if he divorces three, then three."
"18379","(18379) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Masruq, who said: A man came to Omar and said: I am I placed my wife’s affairs in her hands, so she divorced herself three times. Omar said to Abdullah: What do you say? Abdullah said: He saw it as one, and he owned it. Omar said: I also see that."
"18380","(18380) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Jafar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aban bin Uthman, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit; That he said about a man who said to his wife: If you cross the threshold of this door, then I command you with your own hand. She passed and divorced herself. Many divorces. Zaid said: She is one."
"18381","(18381) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ghaylan ibn Jarir, on the authority of Abu Al-Halal Al-Atkiki; He came to Othman and said: I said: A man who has put the affairs of his wife in her hands. He said: So he has put his affairs in her hands."
"18382","(18382) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Talha Shaddad, on the authority of Ghaylan ibn Jarir, on the authority of Abu al-Halal, he said: I asked Uthman About a man who puts his wife’s affairs in his hands? He said: The judgment is as long as it has been decided."
"18383","(18383) Ibn Abi Zaydah and Ali Ibn Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The judgment is what it has decided."
"18384","(18384) Ibn Abi Zayed told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The judgment is what it has decided."
"18385","(18385) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Fadalah bin Ubaid (h) and on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abd His Lord, on the authority of Abu Iyad, he said: The decree is what it has decreed."
"18386","(18386) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: The judiciary is what it has decided."
"18387","(18387) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; Concerning a man who put his wife’s affairs in his hand, so she divorced herself three times. He said: Three times."
"18388","(18388) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; Concerning a man who puts his wife’s affairs in his hand, he said: The decree is what she has decreed, so if they deny it, he must swear an oath."
"18389","(18389) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, and al-Zuhri, who said: The decree is what it has decided."
"18390","(18390) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I said to the arbitrator: She said: Have I divorced myself three times? He said: It has been cleared of it with three, meaning if he puts her affairs in his hands."
"18391","(18391) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, on the authority of Abdullah; That a man put the matter of his wife in her hand, so she divorced herself three times. He said: One. Then he met Omar and said: What a good thing. I saw you"
"18392","(18392) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, he said: It was narrated to us then that Omar bin Abd al-Aziz wrote about a man From the Banu Tamim who put his wife’s affairs in her hand, he said: If she returns the matter to him, then nothing is wrong, and if she divorces herself, then there is nothing wrong with her. One, and He has more right to it."
"18393","(18393) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Concerning a man who said to his wife: Your command is in your own hands, and she said: You are divorced three times. Ibn Abbas said: May God forgive her whims. She said: I have been divorced three times. It would have been as she said."
"18394","(18394) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, he said: I mentioned it to Abraham, and he said: Both are one and the same. I have control over her if she says: I divorce you, or I divorce myself."
"18395","(18395) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: May God make her mistake."
"18396","(18396) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Concerning a man who put his wife’s affairs in his hand, and she said: You are divorced three times. He said: May God make her whine wrong."
"18397","(18397) Muhammad bin Bishr Al-Abdi narrated to us, saying: Zakaria bin Abi Zaydi narrated to us, saying: Mansour narrated to me, saying: Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, said: I was with Abdullah bin Masoud when a man came to him and said: O Abu Abdul Rahman, he is There was some disagreement between me and my family, and she said: If whatever matter is in your hand were in my hand Do you know what I do? So I said to her: It is in your hand. She said: I have divorced you three times. Abdullah said: This is one divorce, and you I have more right to her. He said: Then I mentioned that to Omar, and he said: If you had said otherwise, I would have seen that you were not injured."
"18398","(18398) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Abdullah said: If a man gives the choice to his wife So she chooses herself, then one is certain, and if she chooses her husband, then nothing matters. Ali said: If she chooses herself One is irrevocable, and if she chooses her husband then one, and he has the right to take her back."
"18399","(18399) Ali bin Musahir narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, who said: I do not care if I give my wife the choice. One, or a hundred, or a thousand, after you chose me, and I came to Aisha and asked her about that? She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave us a choice and we chose him. Was it a divorce? (Bukhari 5263 and Muslim 1154)"
"18400","(18400) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Bishr, he said: I heard Ikrimah speaking; Abu Al-Darda’ came while he was in the Levant about a man who gave his wife the choice and she chose her husband. He said: It is nothing. He said: And it was Ibn Abbas issued a fatwa on that, and Aban bin Uthman ruled on it in Medina."
"18401","(18401) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Musa bin Muslim, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Ali said: If a man takes off his His wife from his neck, then she is one, even if she chooses him."
"18402","(18402) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Issa bin Asim, on the authority of Zazan, he said: We were sitting with Ali, He was asked about the option? He said: The Commander of the Faithful Omar asked me about her, and I said: If she chooses herself, then one is certain, and if she chooses her husband So one, and he has more right to her. He said: It is not as you said: If she chooses herself, then one, and he has more right to her, even if She chose her husband and nothing matters, and he has more right to her, so I found no alternative but to follow the Commander of the Faithful. When I was appointed and went to private parts, I returned to what I knew, and it was said to him: Your opinion in congregation is more beloved to us than What is your opinion about the group? Ali laughed and said: Did he not send to Zayd ibn Thabit and ask him? He said: If she chooses herself, then three, and if she chooses her husband, then one definitive person."
"18403","(18403) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who says to his wife: Choose me. He said: If she chooses herself, then one, and if she chooses her husband, then nothing."
"18404","(18404) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, He said: If she chooses herself, then three, and if she chooses her husband, then one."
"18405","(18405) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad, on the authority of Kharijiyah ibn Zaid, and Aban ibn Uthman, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit said: If she chooses herself, then one, and he has control over her, and if she chooses her husband, then nothing."
"18406","(18406) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God gave us a choice. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so we chose him, but he did not promise us anything. (Bukhari 5262. Muslim 28)"
"18407","(18407) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I asked Abu Ja’far about A man gives his wife a choice, so she chooses her husband? He said: It is nothing. I said: So if she herself chooses? He said: I divorce him, but he is more deserving of taking her back."
"18408","(18408) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab; Concerning a man who gave his wife the choice, and she returned that to him, but she did not fulfill anything on her behalf. He said: That is nothing."
"18409","(18409) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He used to say about the option, like what Omar and Abdullah said."
"18410","(18410) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Omar, and Abdullah; They both said: Your command is in your hand and your choice is the same."
"18411","(18411) Hafs told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, who said: In their saying, “Your command is in your hand and you choose.” Either way"
"18412","(18412) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali, and Abdullah, And Zaid, they said: Your command is in your hand and choose, whether it is the same."
"18413","(18413) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, they said: Your command With your hand and choose, all the same."
"18414","(18414) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham; It has reached him that Omar bin Abdul Aziz has put your affairs in your hands and chosen you, regardless of whether."
"18415","(18415) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, who said: If a man gives the choice to his wife, then What did she say in their gathering? If they separate, then nothing matters."
"18416","(18416) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Al-Muthanna, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather; Omar bin Al-Khattab and Othman bin Affan said: Whichever man makes his wife king, he commands her, or he gives her the choice, so they parted after that. She did not say anything about it, so he sent her matter to her husband."
"18417","(18417) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Abdullah said: When he made A man commanded his wife in the hands of a man, and he got up before he had decided anything about it, so he had no command."
"18418","(18418) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: If a man gives the choice to his wife, She did not choose that in her session, so she has no choice."
"18419","(18419) Ibn Ayyash told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, who said: If a man gives his wife a choice, then if she chooses, Otherwise, she does not have the right to choose whatever she wants."
"18420","(18420) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: When she rises from her seat Nothing"
"18421","(18421) Yahya bin Bashir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, and Amr bin Dinar, who said: When they separated in Ownership and choice, she has no choice."
"18422","(18422) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Abdullah bin Amr; Concerning a man who gives his wife a choice. He said: That is hers as long as she remains in her court."
"18423","(18423) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid; Concerning a man who gives his wife a choice, they said: If she gets up from her seat before she makes her choice, then she has no choice."
"18424","(18424) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to me, on the authority of Amer, who said: If a man gives the choice His wife did not choose that sitting, so she has no choice in that matter."
"18425","(18425) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali; Concerning a man who puts the affairs of his wife in her hand, he said: She is not allowed to speak, or he puts the affairs of his wife in the hands of a man, he says: He With his hand until he speaks."
"18426","(18426) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salma, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muslim; That a man put his wife’s affairs in her hands, so she got up and did not fulfill anything. It was brought to Ibn al-Zubayr, and he said: What did you do? She said: I must not return to him, so he told her about it."
"18427","(18427) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Concerning a man who gave his wife the choice, saying: He has the right to take her back unless she speaks."
"18428","(18428) Omar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd, who said: He has that."
"18429","(18429) Omar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who gives his wife a choice, or puts her affairs in her hands, then rejects that before she says anything. He said: That's why"
"18430","(18430) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Ibn Masoud said: If a man gives his wife a choice, and she gets up from her seat, then there is no matter for her, but if he takes her back before she makes her choice, then there is nothing for her. No"
"18431","(18431) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: If he gave her the choice Three times, so she chose three times."
"18432","(18432) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; Concerning a man who gave his wife the choice three times, and she herself chose one time. He said: She made it clear of him three times."
"18433","(18433) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: He was asked about a man who said: To his wife: Choose me, so she remained silent. Then he said: Choose me, so she remained silent. Then he said: Choose me. So she chose herself at the third time? So he made it clearer, so he made it three."
"18434","(18434) It was narrated on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When he gave her three choices, she chose Mara. There are three"
"18435","(18435) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: She remained silent, content with the husband. If he gave her a choice, she remained silent."
"18436","(18436) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Her silence is pleasing to the husband."
"18437","(18437) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Jarir bin Hazim narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Sa’id, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ali bin Yazid bin Rukaniya, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather; That he divorced his wife immediately, so he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him? He said: What did you want with it? He said: One. He said: By God, I only wanted one with her? He said: By God, I did not want it except one. He said: So return it to him. (Abu Dawud 2011, Bayhaqi 342)"
"18438","(18438) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ali, who said: There are three."
"18439","(18439) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; In fact, three divorces."
"18440","(18440) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Omar, and Abdullah, who said: He divorced him, and he I own it."
"18441","(18441) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abbad, on the authority of Al-Muttalib bin Hantab, on the authority of Omar; He made the wife a divorce, and her husband took possession of her."
"18442","(18442) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Salamah, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yasar (h) On the authority of Ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, on the authority of Omar; Like him"
"18443","(18443) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, on the authority of Omar; Concerning a man saying to his wife, “You are absolutely divorced,” she is definitely single. Ali said: “Three,” and Shurayh said: We support him with his heresy."
"18444","(18444) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Abdullah ibn Shaddad testified with Urwah ibn Al-Mughirah, that Omar made them one, and he has more right to her, and that Al-Raish bin Adiy bore witness to Ali, that he made them three. And Shurayh said: His intention."
"18445","(18445) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: When he sent Urwa to Shurayh, he became arrogant and determined to attack him. On him, they would say, and he said: Indeed, God has enacted Sunnahs, and people have innovated, and they have resorted to their innovations and mixed them with Sunnahs. So if you come across anything of that, then distinguish the Sunnahs and implement them according to their proper meaning, and attach the innovations to their proper owners. He is divorced: then it is common for him, and as for the divorced person: then he is an heresy who stops his heresy, so if he wants, he can move forward, and if he wants, he can delay it."
"18446","(18446) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’; That Ibn Omar brought his husband to Asim bin Omar and Ibn al-Zubayr, and he said: This husband of yours has divorced his wife absolutely. Before he entered into it, do you have any knowledge of that? Or can you find a concession for him? They said: No, but we left Ibn Abbas and Abu Hurairah with Aisha, so come to them and ask them, then return to us. So he informed us, so he came to them and asked them? Abu Hurairah said: She is not permissible for her until she marries another husband. Ibn Abbas said: She has spent the night, and he mentioned from Aisha. following them."
"18447","(18447) A partner told us, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Saeed; Of course: If he intends one, then one, and if he intends three, then three."
"18448","(18448) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he intends a divorce, then the minimum will be. His intention in that matter is one and clear. If he wishes and she wishes, he may marry her, and if he intends to do so, then three."
"18449","(18449) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He will be asked about his intention."
"18450","(18450) Hatim bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhul, who said: There are three."
"18451","(18451) Ismail bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Ubaid, on the authority of Makhoul, and Al-Zuhri, who said: Three."
"18452","(18452) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: Abu Bakr said: Omar bin Abd asked me Al-Aziz forever? So I said to him: Aban bin Uthman used to say: One, so Omar said: If the divorce had been a thousand times, she would not have kept the divorce. Something from it."
"18453","(18453) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Hazm, he said: He said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz: O Abu Bakr, of course, what do people say about it? So I said to him: Aban bin Uthman used to make her one, and Omar said: If the divorce had been a thousand times, she would not have kept it as a divorce. Something, whoever says absolutely, has committed the ultimate goal."
"18454","(18454) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of his leaders; Zayd bin Thabit used to say at all: three."
"18455","(18455) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Omar, and Abdullah, who said: In the cell. He divorced her, and he has the right to take her back."
"18456","(18456) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Kurdous, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah; In the cell, he said: His intention."
"18457","(18457) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ali, who said: There are three."
"18458","(18458) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: There are three."
"18459","(18459) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Wahib, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: Intention"
"18460","(18460) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning the marriage: If he intends a divorce, the minimum is an irrevocable divorce. If she wishes, he may marry her, even if he intends to divorce her three times. Then three"
"18461","(18461) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Omar, and Abdullah; Concerning Al-Bariyah: They said: Divorce him, and he is in control of her."
"18462","(18462) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ali, who said: There are three."
"18463","(18463) Hushaym bin Bashir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There are three."
"18464","(18464) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: He used to say: It is one and the same."
"18465","(18465) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It is as he said."
"18466","(18466) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If one person intends, then one, and if If he intends two, then two, and if he intends three, then three."
"18467","(18467) Hatim bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhul; In Al-Bariyya, he said: Three."
"18468","(18468) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Wahib, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; In the wilderness, he said: He did not intend."
"18469","(18469) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Minhal Al-Tai’i, who said: I asked Al-Shu’abi about a man who said to his wife: “I am free from you?” He said: His intention."
"18470","(18470) Zayd ibn Harun told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr, who said: Jabir ibn Zayd was asked about a man with whom she had intercourse. His wife asked him for divorce, and he said: Go away, for I am free from you, and you are free from me, and does he not intend to divorce then? He said: If he did not intend to divorce, then it is not a divorce, but if he intended to divorce, then it is one, and he has the right to review it in the matter. I counted it"
"18471","(18471) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; He said in Al-Bariyyah: If he intends to divorce, then the minimum of his intention in that matter is one and clear, if she so desires and so desires. He marries her, and if he intends three, then three."
"18472","(18472) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: There are three things that are not permissible for him even She marries another husband."
"18473","(18473) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders; Zayd ibn Thabit used to say: There are three types of barayah."
"18474","(18474) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Omar, and Abdullah; In the case of an irrevocable divorce, he has the right to take her back."
"18475","(18475) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ali, who said: There are three."
"18476","(18476) Hatim bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhul; Concerning Al-Ba’in, he said: These are three."
"18477","(18477) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Wahib, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; In the clear: what he intended."
"18478","(18478) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; In Al-Ba’inah: three."
"18479","(18479) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The clear is three, no She is permissible for him until she marries another husband."
"18480","(18480) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders; Zayd bin Thabit used to say about Al-Ba’inah: Three."
"18481","(18481) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Na’im bin Dajjajah; Concerning a man who divorced his wife twice, then he said: You are burdened by me, so Omar said: This is not our right."
"18482","(18482) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Khalas, and Abu Hassan; Ali used to say: Three. His followers said: This was the opinion of Al-Hasan, so he issued a fatwa based on it."
"18483","(18483) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; Concerning a divorce of embarrassment: three."
"18484","(18484) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Wahib, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; Concerning divorce of embarrassment: what he intended."
"18485","(18485) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders; That Ali said regarding the difficult divorce: Three times. He said: And so did Al-Hasan."
"18486","(18486) Hatem bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, who said: If a man says to his wife: You It is forbidden for me, so there are three things."
"18487","(18487) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ali, who said: Three."
"18488","(18488) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Amer, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: It is forbidden if he intends a single divorce. He has the right to take her back, and if he does not intend to divorce her, then he has an oath to expiate her."
"18489","(18489) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Abu Ja`far; Like him"
"18490","(18490) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah; In the forbidden: If he intends to make an oath, then he will keep it, and if he intends to divorce, then he does not intend."
"18491","(18491) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abd al-Khaliq, on the authority of Hammad, who said: The forbidden is one and the same."
"18492","(18492) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man says to his wife: It is forbidden to me. He intends to divorce, so the minimum is an irrevocable divorce."
"18493","(18493) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he intends to divorce, then the minimum of his intention is to That is one single woman, if he wants and she wants, he can marry her, but if he intends to do three, then three."
"18494","(18494) Abd al-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, on the authority of Sa`d bin Hisham; Zayd bin Thabit said: These are three, and she is not permissible for him until she marries another husband."
"18495","(18495) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of his followers; Zayd bin Thabit used to say about what is forbidden: three."
"18496","(18496) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Omar, who said: The forbidden is right."
"18497","(18497) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Omar; Like him"
"18498","(18498) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha, that she said: Right."
"18499","(18499) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas (h) and on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd. And Saeed bin Jubayr, Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, and Suleiman bin Yasar; They said: The forbidden is the right."
"18500","(18500) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: I do not care whether it is forbidden, or water. Furata"
"18501","(18501) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ata’ and Tawus, who said: Right."
"18502","(18502) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaab, he said: Some people said: Three, and others said: Infidels. Right, and I see that he must make expiation for zihar."
"18503","(18503) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id (h) and Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, who said: The forbidden is the right."
"18504","(18504) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: It was narrated to me by someone who did not Atham, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The forbidden is right, (God has made it obligatory for you to be permissible) Your faith)"
"18505","(18505) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhul, and Sulayman bin Yassar, who said: The forbidden is right."
"18506","(18506) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, who said: I do not care whether you forbid it, or I forbid it. A handful of porridge."
"18507","(18507) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of al-Dahhak; Abu Bakr, Omar, and Ibn Masoud said: Whoever says to his wife: It is forbidden to him, it is not forbidden to him. And he has to make expiation for swearing an oath."
"18508","(18508) Abduh bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: If a man says to his wife: You are my wife It is forbidden, so it is nothing."
"18509","(18509) Ali told us, on the authority of Ismail, he said: Amer said: Some people claimed that Ali had made it forbidden to him. Until she marries another husband, and by God, Ali has never said that about me, and I know more about it than the one who said it? He only said: I do not make it permissible for him, nor do I make it forbidden to him. If he wishes, let him advance, and if he wishes, let him delay."
"18510","(18510) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr; Concerning a man who says to his wife: You are sacred to me. He said: He will free a slave, and if he says that for four, then four slaves."
"18511","(18511) Ibn Ayyash told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who said: Everything that is permissible for me is forbidden. He said: Were it not for his wife, I would have commanded him to make expiation for his oath."
"18512","(18512) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, who said: I asked Al-Sha’bi about a man who said: Everything that is permissible for me is forbidden? He said: It does not necessitate divorce, nor does it make lawful forbidden, it expiates his oath."
"18513","(18513) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he says: Everything permissible for me is forbidden, if he intends A divorce, then it is a divorce, and he is in control of her, and if he does not intend a divorce, then there is an oath to expiate her."
"18514","(18514) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, who said: If he says: Everything permitted to me is forbidden, then he feeds ten Poor people"
"18515","(18515) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawwi, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of al-Hasan, and Jabir ibn Zaid They said: Everything permitted to me is forbidden, an expiation for an oath."
"18516","(18516) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Saleh, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ali; Concerning a man who says to his wife: Everything that is permissible for me is forbidden. He said: His wife is forbidden to him, and it is not permissible for him until she gets married. A different husband, and he will make amends for his oath with his wealth."
"18517","(18517) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah; Concerning a man who gifts his wife to her family, he said: If her family accepts her and she divorces her, then she is king, you can take her back, but if not They accept it and nothing happens."
"18518","(18518) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If they accept her and she is divorced, he will have the right to take her back."
"18519","(18519) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Yahya bin Wattab, some of our companions said: It is on the authority of Masruq, On the authority of Abdullah, he said: If a man says to his wife: Be happy with your command, or choose it, or I have given you to your family, then Divorce"
"18520","(18520) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: If they accept it, then one is clear, and if they do not accept it, then one, and he has more right to take it back."
"18521","(18521) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of al-Hasan, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: Then he granted it. So they accepted her, then three, she is not lawful for her until she marries another husband, and if they reject her, then one, and that is more deserving Through it, and through it, good deeds were taken."
"18522","(18522) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who married a woman and then gave her to her family. Ata’ said: If they accept her, it is an irrevocable divorce. They returned it and nothing happened."
"18523","(18523) Yunus bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos; Concerning the woman who repented to her family: a divorce, and he is more deserving of her taking her back."
"18524","(18524) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Jazzar, on the authority of Ali ; Concerning the gift to her family: If they accept her, then they divorce her permanently, and if they return her, then it is one divorce, and that is more deserving. With it"
"18525","(18525) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Jazzar, on the authority of Ali; In a similar way"
"18526","(18526) Waki` narrated to us: If he promised her to her family and he did not intend to divorce her, then they would accept it. Or they reject her, and if he intends a divorce, then whatever divorce he intends, they accept it, or they reject her."
"18527","(18527) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hamid al-Tawil, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: A woman said to her husband: Give me relief. God is from you. Hamid said: Or something like this. He said: So he said: Yes. So yes. So yes. He said: Then Omar bin Al-Khattab came and mentioned. That is for him, so Omar said: Do you want me to bear it for you? Here you are, here you are, here you are."
"18528","(18528) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Ali bin Omar bin Hussein, on the authority of Jafar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali; Concerning a man who divorced his wife after carrying a camel, he said: She is not lawful for him until she marries another husband."
"18529","(18529) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Asid, on the authority of Arfaja, on the authority of Aisha; Concerning a man who divorced his wife once or twice, she said: She is not lawful for him until she marries another husband."
"18530","(18530) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who divorces his wife three times and then denies her. He said: I would love for you to take her to the authority. If he swore, I would love for you to You will ransom yourself from him if he swears an oath."
"18531","(18531) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If she is truthful, then it is permissible for her to pay a ransom."
"18532","(18532) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: You bring him to the Sultan and ask him to take an oath."
"18533","(18533) Jarir told us, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Taymi, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a woman who claims that her husband divorced her three times and she has no legal guardian between her. He said: He commanded her to confess with him but he did not flee"
"18534","(18534) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Jabir bin Zayd, who said: They had not committed adultery together."
"18535","(18535) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Ibn Umar was a captive, Her husband was reluctant to divorce her, so she said to Ibn Omar: He would have something to do with him in secret, so he swore to her and left him."
"18536","(18536) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hudhayl bin Bilal, on the authority of a sheikh whose nickname was: Abu Amr, who said: I was sitting with Ibn Abbas, when a woman came to him and said: Her husband is divorcing her in secret and denies her in public. He said: He must swear four testimonies to God that he will not divorce him, and the fifth is that God’s curse will be upon him if he does so."
"18537","(18537) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of al-Hakam ibn Atiyya, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Sirin, and he was asked about A man divorces his wife three times, then denies her? He said: Run away from him."
"18538","(18538) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: You should ask him to swear after the prayer, and if he swears, it will be answered."
"18539","(18539) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad, who said: I asked him about a man who divorced his wife three times, and she was not hers. Clear? He said: She ransoms herself with her wealth. He said: I said: And if he refuses? He said: Flee from it and do not compare it."
"18540","(18540) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Siwar, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: There was an order like this: that you flee."
"18541","(18541) Muhammad bin Marwan told us, on the authority of Amara, who said: Jabir bin Zaid was asked about a man who made the mistake of divorcing his wife? He said: There is no fault on the believer."
"18542","(18542) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, and Al-Hakam; Concerning a man who wanted to say something, but he made a mistake and divorced, and Al-Sha’bi said: It is nothing, and Al-Hakam said: He is bound to him."
"18543","(18543) Abd al-Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man divorces his wife once, irrevocably, it falls He must divorce her as long as it was during the waiting period."
"18544","(18544) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; Concerning a man who divorces his wife irrevocably, then follows up with a divorce within her waiting period. He said: His divorce applies to her as long as she was In the iddah"
"18545","(18545) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; Like him"
"18546","(18546) Abu Issam Rawad bin Al-Jarrah told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Makhul, and Ata’; Concerning a man who divorces his wife once and for all, then he divorces her during her waiting period. They said: The divorce counts as a divorce."
"18547","(18547) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: The divorced woman must be divorced in The number"
"18548","(18548) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh; Like him"
"18549","(18549) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi (h) and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They are required to divorce each other during the waiting period."
"18550","(18550) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: Ali said: Divorce and iddah with women."
"18551","(18551) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The Sunnah for a woman in divorce, or The number"
"18552","(18552) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Divorce and the iddah with wives."
"18553","(18553) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad, that they both said: Divorce and iddah with women."
"18554","(18554) Ismail Ibn Ali told us, on the authority of Ayoub, who said: I was informed on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Like that"
"18555","(18555) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: The slave woman is distinguished from the free man and the slave by two divorces."
"18556","(18556) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Saif, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If the mother is under the heat, then there are two divorces. Her waiting period is two menstrual cycles, and if the free woman is married to the slave, then her divorce is three menstruation periods, and her waiting period is three menstruation periods."
"18557","(18557) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Suleiman Ibn Yasar; Nufia, a young man from Umm Salama, divorced his wife while she was a free woman and had been divorced twice. They were keen to return her to him, but he refused. Othman and Zaid. Suleiman said: And anyone says other than this? When I came to Medina, I wrote to Abu Qalabab, and he wrote to me: Someone whose hadith I was confident about told me: Zayd bin Thabit and Qubaisa bin Dhu’ib said: If her husband is free and he is a mother, then her divorce is a free divorce, and her waiting period is The iddah of a mother, and if her husband is a slave and she is free, then her divorce is the divorce of a slave, and her iddah is the iddah of a free woman."
"18558","(18558) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: Abdullah narrated to me, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Yasar, he said: Divorce with men And the number of women."
"18559","(18559) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah; Like him"
"18560","(18560) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas (h) and on the authority of al-Sha`biy, on the authority of Makhoul (H) and Sufyan, on the authority of those who heard Ibrahim and Al-Sha’bi, who said: Divorce with men, and the waiting period with women."
"18561","(18561) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salama, who said: Nafi’ narrated to us. He was a slave and there was a free woman under him, so he divorced her twice, so he asked Uthman and Zaid? They said: Your divorce is the divorce of a slave, and you counted it as a free woman."
"18562","(18562) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: If the free woman is under the slave So she has performed the period with two divorces, and her iddah has been three menstrual periods, and if the mother is under the heat, then she has performed it with three menstrual periods. I promised her two menstrual cycles."
"18563","(18563) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, who said: Divorce is for men, and the waiting period For women"
"18564","(18564) Abu Muawiyah and Abu Asamah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah said: Sell a slave woman. Her divorce"
"18565","(18565) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan (h) and on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu, who said: Selling a mother to divorce her."
"18566","(18566) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, Jabir, and Anas. They said: Sell slave women. Her divorce"
"18567","(18567) Abdou told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Whichever of them was sold, that is his. Divorce"
"18568","(18568) Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Ali bin Hakim, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Whichever of them was sold, then that one. No divorce"
"18569","(18569) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: A portion of it in the sale of either of them. It was"
"18570","(18570) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He sold her divorce."
"18571","(18571) Ali told us, on the authority of Ismail, he said: I asked Amir about a man who bought a newborn woman and she had a husband. He would have sexual intercourse with her. ? He said: If he had intercourse with her, it would not have changed that for anyone. He said: And if he were to be freed from it, it would be better for him."
"18572","(18572) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If the slave-mother is sold, or given away, or She inherited, or was emancipated, this is a separation."
"18573","(18573) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salama; That Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf bought a slave girl from Asim ibn Adi, and he was informed that she had a husband, so he returned her."
"18574","(18574) Abd ibn Sulayman told us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Sulayman ibn Yasar; Asim bin Adiy gave Abd al-Rahman bin Awf a maid, and when he approached her, she informed him that she had a husband, so he returned her. Aliyah"
"18575","(18575) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Saad, on the authority of Yasar bin Nimir, on the authority of Omar, who said: He bought a few."
"18576","(18576) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Saad; That Saad bought a slave girl who had a husband, and he did not approach her until he had bought some of her from her husband for five hundred."
"18577","(18577) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Saad; That Saad married his slave-girl whom he owned, so she followed her. He said: So he made a burden for his servant to divorce her."
"18578","(18578) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’; That a man gave a gift to Uthman as a slave, and when he stripped her, she said: I have a husband, so he returned her to her master, and said: I gave you a gift. She has a maid who has a husband."
"18579","(18579) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: A man from Hamdan gave Ali the gift of guidance. A neighbor, and when she came to him, Ali asked her: Are you free or busy? She said: She is busy, O Commander of the Faithful. He said: So he separated from her and sent to her husband and bought some of her from him for ten. And four hundred"
"18580","(18580) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The slave has more right to his wife. Wherever he finds her, unless he divorces her irrevocably."
"18581","(18581) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: I was informed that Abdul Rahman saw A woman liked him, so he asked about her? They said: This is the mother of so-and-so, so he bought her for four thousand dirhams, and when she had a husband, he gave him a hundred dirhams for it. To divorce her, but he refused, so he added more money, but he refused, so he increased it, but he refused, until he reached five hundred dirhams, but he refused, so he returned it to him."
"18582","(18582) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ma’abad ibn Khalid, or on the authority of Abu Husayn; That Abu Masoud hated to have intercourse with her when she had a husband."
"18583","(18583) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: Indeed, I would hate to have intercourse with a woman’s private parts, if I found a man with her whom I did not punish."
"18584","(18584) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan and Ali bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Qays bin Wahhab al-Hamdani, on the authority of Abu Salam bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Awf; He hated having intercourse with her when she had a husband. Ali bin Saleh added to it: Abd al-Rahman bin Awf said: Two spouses are not reconciled in Islam."
"18585","(18585) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulaiman, on the authority of Anas ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Umar; That Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf bought a female slave who had a husband, and he said: He returned her to her, and said: She was given to me by permission."
"18586","(18586) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid al-Makki, on the authority of Salim, al-Qasim, and Ubaid Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Omar, they said: Omar said: Divorce is in the hands of the one for whom it is permissible to be separated."
"18587","(18587) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Abu Saeed bin Awdh, who said: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr asked by a man, and he said: Did my female slave marry my slave? Then I wanted to separate them? He said: You are not allowed to do that."
"18588","(18588) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the master gives permission, then divorce is in the hands of the slave."
"18589","(18589) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If he marries with his master’s permission, divorce is in his hands. The slave"
"18590","(18590) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Mubarak bin Fadla, on the authority of Ibrahim Abi Ismail, on the authority of Ali, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and Hudhaifa said about a slave who marries with the permission of his master: divorce is in the hands of the slave."
"18591","(18591) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid who said: If the property belongs to someone else Or she was with him, and he gave him permission to marry her, so divorce is in the hands of the Mamluks."
"18592","(18592) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, who said: I said to my father: A man marries his slave, his slave. Is it right for him to take it away from him without his consent? He said: Evil is what he did."
"18593","(18593) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to say: If a slave marries with his master’s permission, then divorce is in the slave’s hands. If he wants, he can divorce you, and if he wants, he can keep him."
"18594","(18594) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, who said: I said to Sa’id bin Jubayr: Jabir bin Zaid used to say: If The master got married, and the divorce was in his hands, so he said: Jabir bin Zaid lied."
"18595","(18595) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Divorce is in the hands of the one who owns the property."
"18596","(18596) Hatim bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: If a slave marries with the permission of his master, his divorce is subject to A slave, the master has no right to divorce him."
"18597","(18597) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If a man gives his slave in marriage, or gives him permission to marry Divorce is in the hands of the slave."
"18598","(18598) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Juwaybār, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: Whoever marries his male slave to him will pay him a dowry and a clear sum of money, no It is permissible for him to remove her from him, but it is not permissible for him to separate her from her until he dies."
"18599","(18599) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: If the master gives permission to his slave If he gets married, divorce is in the hands of the slave."
"18600","(18600) Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, Ibn Abbas, and Jabir bin Abd. By God, they said: Divorce is in the hands of the master."
"18601","(18601) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: If you marry your slave I made you dead, then you sold him, so you have no right to prevent him."
"18602","(18602) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, and al-Hasan. They said: So The slave got married with his master’s permission, so divorce is in the slave’s hands."
"18603","(18603) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Amir, who said: If a slave marries without his master’s permission, then divorce is In the hand of her master"
"18604","(18604) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a slave who marries without his master’s permission, he said: If the master wishes, he can cancel it, and if he wishes, he can remain silent."
"18605","(18605) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If a slave marries without permission His master, then divorce is in the hands of the master, and if he marries with his permission, then divorce is in the hands of the slave."
"18606","(18606) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Umari narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, the same."
"18607","Abu Abdul Rahman Buqiy bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Abu Bakr Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abi Shayba told us, he said:\n(18607) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Ikrim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: If you embrace Christianity, Before her husband, she owned herself."
"18608","(18608) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of his father; Al-Hasan and Omar bin Abdul-Aziz said about Christianity being that she becomes a Muslim under her husband. They said: Islam expelled her from it."
"18609","(18609) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning Christianity, she is married to her husband. He said: He will separate them."
"18610","(18610) Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata, Tawoos, and Mujahid; Concerning a Christian woman, there is a Christian woman under her and she converts to Islam. They said: If he converts to Islam with her, then he is his wife, but if he does not convert to Islam, then he is separated. Between them."
"18611","(18611) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Saffah bin Matar, on the authority of Dawud bin Kurdous, who said: There was a man From the Banu Tamim, it is said to him: Abaad bin Al-Numan bin Zur’a. He has a wife from Banu Tamim, and he was Abaad. He was a Christian, so his wife converted to Islam and he refused to convert to Islam, so Omar separated them."
"18612","(18612) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a woman converts to Islam before her husband, her marriage will cease. between them of marriage."
"18613","(18613) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Yazid bin Alqamah; That a man from Banu Tamim defeated him, and he was called: Ubadah bin Al-Numan, and there was under him a woman from Banu Tamim, so she converted to Islam. So Omar called him and said: Either you surrender or I will take it away from you. But he refused to do so, so Omar took it away from him."
"18614","(18614) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Hakam; Concerning a Jew or Christian whose wife surrenders to him, he said: He should separate them."
"18615","(18615) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ibn Shubramah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, who said: I asked Sa’id ibn Jubayr about A Christian man and his wife is Christian, so she converted to Islam? He said: Disperse, disperse."
"18616","(18616) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: He will separate them."
"18617","(18617) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Ali, who said: If a Christian woman converts to Islam, The Jew or Christian had more right to part of it, because he had a covenant."
"18618","(18618) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, and Shu`ba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ali, who said: I have more right to it as long as it remains in the country of Hijra."
"18619","(18619) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Khattimi; Omar wrote: They give us a choice."
"18620","(18620) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, who said: He has more right to her than she was in Egypt."
"18621","(18621) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Their marriage is performed."
"18622","(18622) Waki’ told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hikam; Hani bin Qubaisa Al-Shaybani, who was a Christian and had four wives, so they converted to Islam, so Omar bin Al-Khattab wrote To be steadfast with him."
"18623","(18623) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; That a Christian woman converted to Islam under Christianity, so her family wanted to take her away from him, so they traveled to Omar and he made her a choice."
"18624","(18624) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of his father; Al-Hasan and Omar bin Abdul-Aziz said: His divorce is irrevocable."
"18625","(18625) Abd bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a man and his wife polytheists, so she converted to Islam, but he refused to do so. She broke away from it with one woman, and Ikrimah said the same thing."
"18626","(18626) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The imam’s separation is by divorcing him."
"18627","(18627) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Farwa, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; That the wife of Ikrimah bin Abi Jahl converted to Islam before him, then he converted to Islam while he was in the waiting period, so she was returned to him. This was according to the covenant of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Malik 46)"
"18628","(18628) Abdul bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If he converts to Islam while he is in her waiting period She is his wife."
"18629","(18629) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If he converts to Islam while he is in the waiting period, then he I have more right to it."
"18630","(18630) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: He is more deserving. With it as long as it lasts during the waiting period."
"18631","(18631) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If he converts to Islam while still in the waiting period, then his wife will be his."
"18632","(18632) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, who said: He narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: If the husband converts to Islam after... He gave his wife the choice as long as she was within the waiting period, or he said: He has more right to her as long as she was within the waiting period."
"18633","(18633) Mu’ammar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Whoever is a Jew or a Christian converts to Islam, Then his wife converted to Islam, and they are in a position to marry each other, unless some authority separates them."
"18634","(18634) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, and Al-Hasan that they said: There is no time in Dhahar, and no deity can enter it, even if that lasts for a long time."
"18635","(18635) Abbad told us on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, the same."
"18636","(18636) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who appears from his wife, and does not specify a time limit. He said: His wife does not appear from him. And if he does not intercourse with her, then He always blames himself for atonement."
"18637","(18637) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no time in zihaar."
"18638","(18638) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no time in zihaar."
"18639","(18639) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: There is no time for zihaar."
"18640","(18640) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Concerning a man who said to his wife: If you approach her for a year, then he will be rewarded like his mother’s back. He said: Then Al-Sha’bi said: The Ila’a does not enter. Outwardly"
"18641","(18641) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Al-Hikam and Hammad, who said: If a man says to his wife: He lived on his mother’s back for four months, then four months passed and he was a deity, and when he said: “Ali” Like my mother’s appearance, and he left her for a year, so it is not loyalty."
"18642","(18642) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ali, who said: He does not enter Ilaa in Zhahar, and there is no Zhahar in Ilaa."
"18643","(18643) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no time for zihaar, except when He says: I am close to you, but if he says that he leaves her for four months, then he will not be able to receive it."
"18644","(18644) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Salem, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: If a man says to his wife: “You are my wife.” My mother, if I bring her close to you, then if he brings her close to her, he will abstain from it, and if he leaves her for four months, then it will be clear of loyalty to her."
"18645","(18645) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: It is Ilaa."
"18646","(18646) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who said to his wife: If I approach you, then you will be upon me like my mother’s back, and he left her for four months. He said: Not With something"
"18647","(18647) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of al-Hasan (h) and on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Abraham said: If a man says to his wife: If I bring you near, then you are to me like a mother’s back, then if he offers her near within the four months So it is zihar, and it has been proven, and if he does not approach it until four months have passed, then it is ilaa, and it has disappeared from it. By one"
"18648","(18648) Shabab told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, on the authority of Al-Hikam, and Hammad, who said: I asked them about a man who said to his wife: I have brought you a year, so are you to me like my mother’s back? They said: If four months have passed, then your divorce will be irrevocable, and Abu Bakr will be taken away from it."
"18649","(18649) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Khula is an irrevocable divorce, and divorce is an irrevocable divorce. And the match is the same."
"18650","(18650) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, who said: Ata’ said: Every divorce is a valid marriage, if They are separated in that marriage, and if he does not speak of divorce, then it is one, the marriage is compatible and his ransom is taken."
"18651","(18651) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, he said: I said to Abdul Karim: I was informed that Al-Zuhri used to say: Is marriage more severe than divorce? He said: We do not see him taking something from her as a ransom with it except in the same way as khul’."
"18652","(18652) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Omar bin Amir, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, and Al-Hasan. They said: All A divorce sect."
"18653","(18653) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Every group was formed by men. Divorce"
"18654","(18654) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Every separation entails divorce."
"18655","(18655) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’, on the authority of his followers, who said: Every group will be divorced."
"18656","(18656) Zayd bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Every faction has its own Divorce"
"18657","(18657) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Every sect has a divorce. irrevocable"
"18658","(18658) Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: Not every separation is a divorce."
"18659","(18659) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus (h) and on the authority of Muhammad bin Salem, on the authority of Amer, they said: If the mother is under the heat, and she is freed and chooses herself, then she is separated without divorce."
"18660","(18660) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad (h) and on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If she is freed, she is given the choice. So she chose herself, so they separated without divorce."
"18661","(18661) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It is an irrevocable divorce."
"18662","(18662) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: If she chooses herself, then it is an irrevocable divorce."
"18663","(18663) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who says to his wife: If she wants, then you are divorced. He said: If she wants, then she is divorced, and if she does not want, then nothing."
"18664","(18644) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Hafs bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who said to his wife: You are divorced if you wish. She said: You may wish. He said: He is divorced and he has more right to take you back. Then He said: If you wish, I will divorce you. She said: If you wish, he said: If he wishes, he will not divorce her."
"18665","(18665) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Maimun, the client of the family of Samurah, on the authority of Urwah ibn Faid; That a man said to his wife: If you do such-and-such, you do not have a wife. So she did it, and she went with him to Abd al-Rahman. Ibn Abi Layla, and he said: He did not intend, and she brought with him Abu Abdullah al-Jadali, and he said: He did not intend, and Sa`id bin Jubayr said: Nothing."
"18666","(18666) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Distawai, on the authority of his leaders, who said: I said to Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab: Al-Hajjaj narrates On the authority of his father; That he said about a man who said to his wife: I do not have a wife, and he said: Divorce him, and Sa`id said: How far is that?"
"18667","(18667) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He was asked about a man who said to his wife: Why do you have to have a wife repeatedly when he is angry? Ibrahim said: I do not see him reaching this point unless he wants a divorce."
"18668","(18668) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; He said about a man who said to his wife: I am not married to you. He said: He did not intend to."
"18669","(18669) Muhammad bin Sawa’i told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ata’; Concerning a man who said to his wife: I have no wife. They said: It is a lie, she is nothing."
"18670","(18670) Muhammad bin Sawa’i told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, who said: If he confronts her about him and wants a divorce, then One"
"18671","(18671) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abraham, that he was asked about a man to whom it was said: Do you have a woman? He has a wife, so he said: No, so Abraham said: He told her a lie."
"18672","(18672) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Omar, that he said: A lie; Concerning a man who has a wife and is asked: Do you have a wife? And he says: No."
"18673","(18673) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Sayyar, on the authority of Shu’bi, he said: He is a liar."
"18674","(18674) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam. He said: It is nothing."
"18675","(18675) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan. He said: He is a liar."
"18676","(18676) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who was told: Have you divorced your wife? And he did not do so, so he said: Yes, then he said: The divorce is valid for her."
"18677","(18677) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Abu Hurr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who was told: Have you divorced your wife? He did not divorce her, so he said: Yes, and Al-Hasan said: She has been divorced."
"18678","(18678) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir; Concerning a man who is told: Did you divorce him? And he was not divorced, so he says: Yes, and he says: It is a lie."
"18679","(18679) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ibn Shubarmah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The intention is in what is hidden, but as for what is apparent, then no. His intention therein."
"18680","(18680) Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Dinar, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who divorced his wife once, intending to do so three times, he said: “One.”"
"18681","(18681) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Jafar Al-Ahmar, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: It is one and the same."
"18682","(18682) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hakam; Concerning a man who said to his wife: You are divorced, and he gestured with his hand to three people. He said: So they asked him about that? It was said: She is one."
"18683","(18683) Jarir told us, on the authority of a statement, he said: Al-Sha’bi was asked about the doors to divorce? Al-Sha’bi said: A bitter man was asked: Did you divorce your wife? He said: So he gestured with his hand with four fingers, but did not speak, so he left his wife."
"18684","(18684) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: Cursing is divorce. Clearly"
"18685","(18685) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Cursing is an irrevocable divorce."
"18686","(18686) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: I said to Abraham: The cursed one is more severe than the one who divorces three times? He said: Yes."
"18687","(18687) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Being cursed is more severe than stoning."
"18688","(18688) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, Sulayman bin Yasar, and Hamid bin Abdul Rahman; We heard Abu Hurairah say: I asked Omar about a man from the people of Bahrain who divorced his wife completely, or She was divorced twice and she got married, then her husband divorced her, then the first one married her, how much does she have? He said: For what remains of the divorce."
"18689","(18689) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, and Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Ubi, who said: She returns to him with what remains from the divorce."
"18690","(18690) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Ziyad asked Imran bin Husayn and Shurayh about a man who divorces his wife once, or twice, and it became clear that Then a man marries her and divorces her, or he dies and he marries her first. How long will she be with him? Imran said: For what remains of the divorce, and Shurayh said: A new marriage and a new divorce."
"18691","(18691) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, who said: There were Omar, and Ubayy, and Abu Darda’. And Muadh, they say: You will return to him for what remains."
"18692","(18692) Waki’ and Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Mazid bin Jabir, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Ali, he said: Nothing destroys marriage, except three."
"18693","(18693) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mazid bin Jabir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, who said: Ali What remains?"
"18694","(18694) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of my father, who said: As long as it remains."
"18695","(18695) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, who said: Omar, Muadh, and Zaid passed away. And Ubayy, and Abdullah bin Omar; She is free from the remainder of the divorce."
"18696","(18696) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of Omar, he said: For what remains of the divorce."
"18697","(18697) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: He has a divorce in the future."
"18698","(18698) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, and Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, And Ibn Omar said: He has a new divorce."
"18699","(18699) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham, who said: He has three duties with him."
"18700","(18700) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The companions of Abdullah used to say: Demolish the three, but not It destroys the one and the two, meaning a new divorce."
"18701","(18701) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah’s companions used to say: He will destroy the three. And He does not destroy the one or the two."
"18702","(18702) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Ibrahim; The companions of Abdullah used to say: He destroys one and two just as he destroys three, except for his servants, for he He said: Here it is as long as it remains."
"18703","(18703) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: On a new divorce and on the authority of marriage. New"
"18704","(18704) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of Maimun, who said: He has a new divorce."
"18705","(18705) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Raja’, on the authority of Qubaisya, who said: I said: A man divorced his wife. He divorced him, so she separated from him, so she was divorced, so she married a husband, and he consummated his marriage with her, then he died on her behalf, or he divorced her, so she went back to the first, according to How much does he have? He said: For what remains of the divorce. He said: I said: Then he divorced her again and she divorced him, so she married a husband and he consummated his marriage with her and then he died leaving her, or he divorced her, so she returned to her. Her first husband, how much does she have? He said: Here it is as long as it remains. I said: Then he divorced her from another woman, so she became lawful and married a husband, then he consummated the marriage with her and then he died leaving her, or he divorced her, so she returned to her husband. First, how much does he have? He said: Here are three."
"18706","(18706) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he consummates the marriage with her, then she will be with him for three divorces. If he does not consummate the marriage with her, then she is responsible for the remainder of the divorce."
"18707","(18707) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, who said: He would fall on her at every time of ritual cleansing, then She may keep her until she is pure, then when her pregnancy becomes clear, she will be clear."
"18708","(18708) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; That he said about a man who said to his wife: If she becomes pregnant, then you are divorced. He said: He has intercourse with her when she is pure from menstruation, then He keeps her from her until she becomes pregnant, and Ibn Sirin said: He covers her until she becomes pregnant."
"18709","(18709) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of al-Hasan, Ikrimah, and the letter of Omar ibn Abd al-Aziz They said: If one of them precedes his companion in Islam, then there is no way out for him except by preaching to him."
"18710","(18710) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning the two Magians, if they convert to Islam, then their marriage is in progress. If one of them converts to Islam before his friend, then their marriage is cut off. between them of marriage."
"18711","(18711) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Similar to it, except that he said: It was clear of it."
"18712","(18712) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man and his wife who are polytheists and they surrender. He said: Their marriage is valid. If one of them converts to Islam before The other is that what existed between them was cut off. By that, he means the Magians and polytheists other than the People of the Book."
"18713","(18713) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam; Concerning the Magians: If one of them converts to Islam before his friend, separate them."
"18714","(18714) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, who said: There are three things that should not be played with: marriage, Emancipation and divorce."
"18715","(18715) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Suhaim, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Omar, he said: Four permissible things in any case: emancipation, divorce, marriage, and vow."
"18716","(18716) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Kubran, on the authority of Al-Dahhak; He said: I heard him say: There are three things that should not be played with: divorce, marriage, and vows."
"18717","(18717) Ismail bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Amr bin Muhajir, who said: Abd al-Malik bin Marwan and Suleiman wrote, And Omar bin Abdul Aziz, and Yazid bin Abdul Malik: You do not say anything to the fools, so do not give them divorce or emancipation."
"18718","(18718) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: Three, no games. They include: marriage, divorce, and emancipation."
"18719","(18719) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, he said: The man was in the pre-Islamic era. He divorces and then returns, saying: I was a player. Then he frees him and then returns, saying: I was a player, so God Almighty revealed: {And You take the verses of God as a mockery. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever divorces, or frees, or remarries, or has intercourse, He said that if I was playing, it is permissible. (Tabari 482. Tabrani 780)"
"18720","(18720) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Omar bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Suleiman bin Habib Al-Muharbibi, he said: Omar bin Abdul-Aziz wrote to me: No matter how much you reduce the faiths of the fools, do not deny them freedom. And divorce"
"18721","(18721) Abd ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Saeed, who said: There are three things in which there is no play: emancipation, And divorce, and marriage."
"18722","(18722) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Concerning a man who says to his wife: “He insulted you.” He said: “He divorced you.”"
"18723","(18723) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Divorcing a non-Arab with his tongue is permissible."
"18724","(18724) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Shihab, on the authority of Jabala ibn Da`laj, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, who said: If a man divorces In Persian, he said: It is necessary."
"18725","(18725) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who says to his wife: “He insulted her.” He said: He must divorce her."
"18726","(18726) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who says to his wife: Bashtam, Bhastam, Bhastam. He said: He said it with his tongue. She left him."
"18727","(18727) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, and Ibn Sirin, who said: Khula is not permissible. Until there is a man on her stomach, because God says: {Unless they commit an obvious indecency}"
"18728","(18728) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is not permissible for a man to take a ransom from His wife is not to obey him, nor fulfill an oath to him. If she does that, then something has been done on her part, it is permissible for her to ransom it. If he refuses to accept the ransom from her, and she refuses to obey him, they will send two arbitrators: an arbitrator from his family, and an arbitrator from Welcome"
"18729","(18729) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, who said: If a woman hates her husband, let him take From her and let him leave her."
"18730","(18730) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Marwan Al-Asfar, on the authority of Hamid bin Abdul Rahman Al-Himyari, He said: It is okay for you to take a khula if she says: I will not wash for you from my ritual impurity, nor will I fulfill your oath, nor will I obey your command."
"18731","(18731) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Naji, on the authority of Ali, who said: It is good for a man. Khul’ if she says: I will not perform ablution for you as a part of you, nor will I obey your command, nor will I fulfill my oath to you, nor will I honor any soul."
"18732","(18732) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ali bin Bathimah, on the authority of Miqsam, who said: If she disobeys you and harms you."
"18733","(18733) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Regarding his saying: (There is no impurity) He said: That is in the case of Khula, when she says: I will not perform ablution for you from ritual impurity."
"18734","(۱۸۷۳۴) حَدَّثَنَا ابْنُ فُضَیْلٍ ، عَنْ مُطَرِّفٍ ، عَنْ خَالِدٍ السِّجِسْتَانِیِّ ، عَنِ الضَّحَّاکِ ؛ فِی قولہ تعالی : {لِتَذْہَبُوا بِبَعْضِ مَا آتَیْتُمُوہُنَّ إلاَّ أَنْ یَأْتِینَ بِفَاحِشَۃٍ مُبَیِّنَۃٍ} قَالَ : إذَا فَعَلَتْ ذَلِکَ ، حَلَّ لَہُ To take from her."
"18735","(18735) Ibn Abi Ghani told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who takes off his wife, he said: If that was done by her, then there is no problem."
"18736","(۱۸۷۳۶) حَدَّثَنَا ابْنُ عُلَیَّۃَ ، عَنِ ابْنِ جُرَیْجٍ ، عَنْ عَمْرِو بْنِ دِینَارٍ ، قَالَ : قَالَ جَابِرُ بْنُ زَیْدٍ : إذَا کَانَ Disobedience from before her is permissible for her to be redeemed."
"18737","(۱۸۷۳۷) حَدَّثَنَا ابْنُ عُلَیَّۃَ ، عَنِ ابْنِ جُرَیْجٍ ، عَنْ ہِشَامٍ ؛ That Urwah used to say: It is not permissible for him to ransom him unless the corruption is on her part, and he did not say: It is not permissible for him to sacrifice it. Until you say: I will not fulfill my oath to you, nor will I perform ablution for you in my state."
"18738","(18738) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, who said: Tawoos used to say: It is permissible for him to ransom as long as God said: {except that He feared that he would not uphold the limits of God.} And he did not say the saying of the fools: until you say: I will not wash for you from my necessities, but he He used to say: {except for fear that they will not uphold the limits of God} in what was imposed for each of them on its companion, in the ten And the companions"
"18739","(18739) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, who said: I asked the ruling about a woman’s saying to her husband, “I will not wash for you.” Your honor, I will not honor your oath, nor will I obey your command. He said?? : It's nothing, he keeps it."
"18740","(18740) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, who said: Al-Qasim bin Muhammad was asked: “Unless they fear that they will not maintain limits.” God} said: What was enjoined upon them regarding the ten days and companionship."
"18741","(18741) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Kathir, the servant of Ibn Samurah; Omar was brought to a disobedient woman, and he said to her husband: Take her off."
"18742","(18742) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, Ata’, and Amr bin Shuaib, that they said: Khula is not permissible except for one who is disobedient."
"18743","(18743) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Juman; That a woman was divorced from her husband, so Othman made her a divorce, and so on."
"18744","(18744) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: Jumhan al-Aslami removed a woman, then He regretted it, and she regretted it, so they went to Uthman and mentioned that to him. He said: Uthman said: Yes, she is divorced, unless she named something. It is as you have named it. (Shafi’i 1651, Bayhaqi 316)"
"18745","(18745) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jumhan, on the authority of Uthman, who said: Khula is a divorce."
"18746","(18746) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, who said: My father used to make divorce an irrevocable divorce."
"18747","(18747) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Yazid, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Asim, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, made khula a divorce. (Abdul Razzaq 11758)"
"18748","(18748) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salama, who said: Khula is divorce. Clearly"
"18749","(18749) Waki’, Ibn Uyaynah, and Ali bin Hashim narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah, said: You cannot be an irrevocable divorce, unless it is a ransom or a loyalty, except that Ali bin Hashim He said: On the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah."
"18750","(18750) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and Jabir, on the authority of Amir. (H) And Ata’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, they said: Khul’ is an irrevocable divorce."
"18751","(18751) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Khul’ is an irrevocable divorce, and divorce is an irrevocable divorce. And the match is the same."
"18752","(18752) Abbad told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Saeed bin Al-Musayyab. (h) And Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who divorces his wife. They said: Taking the money is an irrevocable divorce."
"18753","(18753) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Musa ibn Muslim, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Ali said: If a man takes off his wife’s Her neck is one, even if she chooses it."
"18754","(18754) Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Yahya, who said: Qubaysi bin Dhu’ayb said: Khula. Divorce him, if she wants, she can marry him with a new friend."
"18755","(18755) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Every divorce for which a ransom is taken is a divorce, and it is An irrevocable divorce."
"18756","(18756) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: Every divorce is an irrevocable divorce."
"18757","(18757) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Khula is an irrevocable divorce."
"18758","(18758) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It is an irrevocable divorce."
"18759","(18759) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: It is an irrevocable divorce."
"18760","(18760) Omar bin Harun told us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Maymoon, who said: In the readings of Ubayy: Khula is an irrevocable divorce."
"18761","(18761) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhul, who said: Every woman who is ransomed has more right to herself. She should not return to her husband unless You wish"
"18762","(18762) Mukhlid bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: Khula is divorce."
"18763","(18763) Hafs told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed; Othman bin Affan made khula an irrevocable divorce."
"18764","(18764) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salama; He used to say: Khula is an irrevocable divorce."
"18765","(18765) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Khula is an irrevocable divorce, and she did not stipulate that she Divorce is for her."
"18766","(18766) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: It is only a separation and annulment, not By divorce, God mentioned divorce in the beginning of the verses, and in the last verses, and divorce in between, so it is not divorce. God said: {Divorce is twice. So keeping you safe with kindness, or letting go with kindness}"
"18767","(18767) Abd bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab (h) On the authority of Abu Ma`shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, they said: The number of the divorced woman is the number of the divorced woman."
"18768","(18768) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, who said: My father used to say: She observes the waiting period for three menstrual periods, which is I am more likely to propose to her during the waiting period."
"18769","(18769) Jarir and Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Every faction existed between a man. And the woman, her iddah is the same as the divorced woman."
"18770","(18770) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He was saying it"
"18771","(18771) Abdul-Wahhab narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Salim, who said: Her iddah is three menstrual cycles."
"18772","(18772) Waki’ and Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, who said: I counted it as three qari’s."
"18773","(18773) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abd al-A’la, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, on the authority of Ali, who said: He counted The divorced woman is the number of divorced woman."
"18774","(18774) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id, Abu Ayyad, and Khalas. They said: He counted The divorced woman is the number of a divorced woman, and the cursed woman is the number of a divorced woman."
"18775","(18775) Shababi told us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, and Suleiman bin Yasar"
"18776","(18776) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Uthman; He said: The number of divorced women is menstruation."
"18777","(18777) Abdullah told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The count of the woman who has divorced is menstruation."
"18778","(18778) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; Al-Rabi’ah had a divorce from her husband, so her uncle Othman came and said: Should she observe the waiting period for a menstruating woman? He said: She should observe the waiting period for one menstrual period, and Ibn Umar used to say: She should observe the waiting period for three menstrual periods, until Uthman said this, so he used to issue a fatwa based on it. And he says: He is the best of us and the most knowledgeable of us."
"18779","(18779) Muhammad bin Sawa’i told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of Abu Tufayl Sa’id bin Hamal, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said : The number of menstruating women who had divorced, was decided by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding his entire family, Ibn Salul.\n(Abu Dawud 2206 and Abd al-Razzaq 11858)"
"18780","(18780) Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Muharbibi told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Her waiting period is menstruation."
"18781","(18781) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, the client of the family of Talha, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar; Indeed, Al-Rabi’ was removed, so she was ordered to menstruate."
"18782","(18782) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: A divorced woman should observe the waiting period in her husband’s house. Because if he wishes, he can take it back to her."
"18783","(18783) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; Al-Rabi’ah was divorced from her husband, so Mu’awwidh Othman came and asked him, and he said: Will you move? He said: Yes, you will move."
"18784","(18784) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Khaythamiya, who said: Bishr ibn Marwan was brought about a khula’ that was between a man and a woman, but he did not make it up to him, so Abdullah bin Shihab Al-Khawlani said to him: I witnessed Omar bin Al-Khattab being brought to you. There was a divorce between a man and his wife, so he allowed it."
"18785","(18785) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bi, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Shu’bi; Shurayh permitted khula without the authority."
"18786","(18786) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bint Mu’awwidh Ibn Afra’; That her uncle divorced her from her husband, and he was drinking alcohol, not Uthman, so Uthman allowed that."
"18787","(18787) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Khula is permissible without authority."
"18788","(18788) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; He said: Khula is permissible without authority."
"18789","(18789) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, who heard him say: They used to dispossess with us without the authority. If it is submitted to the authority, he will allow it."
"18790","(18790) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He is with the Sultan."
"18791","(18791) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr; Concerning the mukhtal’a, he said: If she is disobedient, the sultan will order him to divorce her."
"18792","(18792) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali ibn al-Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, who said: It was Imran bin Husayn and Ibn Masoud say regarding the woman who ransomes herself from her husband: She has the right to divorce as long as she is in her waiting period."
"18793","(18793) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Fadalah, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Abu Awn al-A'war, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, he said: A divorced woman is entitled to divorce as long as she is in the waiting period."
"18794","(18794) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Yahya, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, he said: Ibn Masoud and Ibn Masoud disagreed. Abbas about a man who divorces his wife and then divorces her. One of them said: His divorce is of no consequence, and the other said: As long as she is in The waiting period, then divorce follows it."
"18795","(18795) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: They will divorce each other."
"18796","(18796) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: She will be divorced as long as She was in the waiting period."
"18797","(18797) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who divorces his wife and then divorces her. He said: His taking of the money is a divorce, and his statement of divorce is a divorce."
"18798","(18798) Abd al-A’la ibn Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, and Khalas, who said: Divorce will apply to her as long as she is in the waiting period."
"18799","(18799) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Khula is an irrevocable divorce, and what follows from the divorce. He will join her as long as she is in the waiting period."
"18800","(18800) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq; Concerning a man who takes his wife off and then divorces her. He said: That is more distant from him than her."
"18801","(18801) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: The divorced woman must be divorced in The number"
"18802","(18802) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi ; In the case of a woman who exonerates her husband and he divorces her, they said: It falls on her as long as she was in her waiting period. Sufyan said: We see that he falls."
"18803","(18803) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning the divorced woman, he said: She is entitled to divorce."
"18804","(18804) Ibn al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, and Ibn al-Zubayr; They both said: It is nothing."
"18805","(18805) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Amr ibn Haram, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zaid; He used to say: His divorce from her does not apply to her, as long as her waiting period was clear."
"18806","(18806) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, and Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning the divorced woman: Divorcing her husband does not count as a divorce as long as she was in a clear waiting period."
"18807","(18807) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: Divorce does not take place as long as she is in the waiting period."
"18808","(18808) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi and Tawus, who said: If he divorced then divorced, he did not Her divorce takes place."
"18809","(18809) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Ikrimah; The divorced woman does not have the right to divorce during her waiting period."
"18810","(18810) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salama, and Ibn Thawban, they said: If he divorces her while he is sitting together, he will be bound to her, otherwise not."
"18811","(18811) Yahya bin Zakariya bin Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: For the deprived of housing and maintenance."
"18812","(18812) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, who said: For the uprooted person there is housing and maintenance. Because if she wanted to, she could marry her husband during her waiting period, she would marry him."
"18813","(18813) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, who said: The woman who has divorced is entitled to maintenance."
"18814","(18814) Waki’ and Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Basri, on the authority of al-Shu’abi; He was asked about a divorced woman: Does she have any maintenance? He said: How can he spend on her when he takes from her?"
"18815","(18815) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to say: Neither the divorced woman nor the divorced woman has three years of residence or maintenance."
"18816","(18816) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’, on the authority of his followers, who said: It is not for the ones who are insolvent and those who are freed. He spent"
"18817","(18817) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: For the kingdom, the one who chooses, and the one who is dislocated, Enjoyment"
"18818","(18818) Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: For the divorced person there is a source of enjoyment."
"18819","(18819) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The deprived have no enjoyment, how can they be entertained? Is he taken from her?"
"18820","(18820) Abdul-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, who said: Every divorced woman has an enjoyment, except for the divorced woman."
"18821","(18821) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: It is not for the uprooted. Enjoyment"
"18822","(18822) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Habib bin Mihran Al-Taymi, who said: I asked Abdullah bin Abi Awfa about A woman divorced her husband with the remainder of the dowry she owed him. Is it permissible for them to take it back? He said: Yes, if he did not mention divorce with a new dowry. He said: And I asked what it was? He said: Yes, even if it is a jug of water."
"18823","(18823) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Amir, and on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man divorces his wife once, on the authority of There is no one who can return when he is a suitor from among the suitors."
"18824","(18824) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: My father used to say: Her companion has the right to propose to her. The number"
"18825","(18825) Abdou told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: When he took it off and then regretted it, it was in it. Iddah, she did not return to him, except with his engagement."
"18826","(18826) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: He should not marry her for less than He took from her."
"18827","(18827) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, who said: I heard Maymoon ibn Mihran say regarding the dislocated people. : If her husband accepts the ransom from her, then proposes to her after that, saying: He will marry her and name a new dowry for her."
"18828","(18828) Ibrahim bin Sadiqa told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In the case of a divorced woman, if her husband wants to take it back, he says: He will propose to her with a new dowry. (Daraqutni 276 Bayhaqi 314)"
"18829","(18829) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; That a woman came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, complaining about her husband. He said: Will you return to him what you took from him? She said: Yes, and more. He said: As for more, no."
"18830","(18830) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali, who said: He does not take from her more than what he gave her."
"18831","(18831) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali; Like him"
"18832","(18832) Abdul Razzaq told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: It is not permissible for him to take from her. More than what he gave her."
"18833","(18833) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Bishr, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: He should not take from her more than He gave it to her, and if he took it, he returned it to her."
"18834","(18834) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated to take from her more than what he had given her."
"18835","(18835) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri and Al-Hasan. They said: It is not taken from her. More than what he gave her."
"18836","(18836) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, Ata’, and Amr bin Shuaib. They said: No. He takes from her her husband except what he gives her."
"18837","(18837) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; He hated to take from her more than what he had given her."
"18838","(18838) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab; He hated to take more than what he gave her."
"18839","(18839) Waki` told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, he said: I asked al-Hakam, and Hammad? He thought that he would take more from her than he had given her."
"18840","(18840) Omar bin Ayyub told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Maymun, who said: Whoever divorces his wife and takes more of her semen from her. Of what He gave her, he did not dispose of it with kindness."
"18841","(18841) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Ammar bin Imran Al-Hamdani, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali; He hated to take from her more than what he had given her."
"18842","(18842) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Raja’ bin Hiyawah; He asked him: How did Al-Hasan say about the infidels? He said: He hated to take from her more than what he had given her, and Raja’ said: Qubaisa bin Dhu’ayb said: Read. The verses that follow it: {And if you fear that you will not keep within the bounds of God, then there is no blame on them for that which you ransom yourself with.}"
"18843","(18843) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Kathir, the servant of Ibn Samurah; Omar brought a disobedient woman, so he ordered her to a house full of dung for three days, then he called her and said: How did you find yourself? She said: I have not had any comfort since I was with him, except for these nights in which I was confined. He said: Take it off, even if it is just a pair of earrings."
"18844","(18844) Affan bin Muslim told us, he said: Hammam told us, he said: Matar told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rabah; Omar said: Depose her for anything less than her punishment."
"18845","(18845) Ali bin Musir told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’; A slave of Safiyya bint Abi Ubaid was removed from her husband with all of her belongings, even some of her clothes. This reached Ibn Umar and he did not deny it."
"18846","(18846) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: You take off until With its punishment"
"18847","(18847) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid; Like him"
"18848","(18848) Waki’ told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham, who said: Even her punishments will be taken from her."
"18849","(18849) Ali bin Hashim narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: There is no harm for a woman to divorce her husband. Even if it is more than what he gave her."
"18850","(18850) Mu’tamar narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man whose wife withdrew herself from him by khula, or sexual intercourse, so he married her, then divorced her before he had intercourse with her. He said: No. Friendship is complete."
"18851","(18851) Yahya bin Zakariya bin Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Ismail, and Ash’ath, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi; In the case of a man who divorces his wife once and for all, then marries her during her waiting period, then divorces her before He entered with her, saying: She has the dowry, and she has a future promise."
"18852","(18852) Ibn Abi Zayed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; The same, and he said: I hope you will return to her."
"18853","(18853) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham; She is entitled to the full dowry, and she is entitled to the full waiting period."
"18854","(18854) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; In the mirror, she separates herself from her husband by one or two divorces, then he marries her, then divorces her before If he consummated the marriage with her, he said: She gets half the dowry."
"18855","(18855) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He was asked about a man who had intercourse with his wife and she divorced him, then he married her during her waiting period, then divorced her before he had intercourse with her? He said: She is entitled to half of the dowry, but she does not have to pay a number."
"18856","(18856) Abdou bin Sulaiman and Muhammad bin Sawa’i told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Ikrimah, And Al-Hasan, they said: If he divorces her, then marries her during her waiting period, then divorces her before consummating the marriage with her, then she gets half the dowry. And she completes the remaining period of waiting."
"18857","(18857) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: She is entitled to half the sadaqa."
"18858","(18858) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of Maimun; Concerning the divorced woman, if her husband accepts the ransom from her, then he proposes to her after that, he says: He will marry her and give her the name. She has a dowry, but if he divorces her before consummating the marriage with her, she gets half the dowry. Ja`far said: And he was not sure of saying: She has a dowry. Friendship is complete."
"18859","(18859) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Harith Al-Ukli; He said: If a woman divorces her husband while he is sick, and then he dies during the waiting period, she has no inheritance."
"18860","(18860) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Like that"
"18861","(18861) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Lahia, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Rabi` al-Qurashi, on the authority of Tubi ibn Nimr, On the authority of Simak Ibn Imran; That Abd al-Malik asked Qabisa about the inheritance of inheritance between divorced women? He said: No, because she ransomed herself with her wealth as perfume."
"18862","(18862) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ata’ al-Khurasani, on the authority of Abu Salama; Othman bin Affan and Zayd bin Thabit said regarding divorce: If four months have passed, then there is a divorce. Amlak by herself."
"18863","(18863) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Qalab; Al-Numan bin Bashir had intercourse with his wife, and Ibn Masoud said: If four months have passed, she has ceased to have intercourse with him. By divorcing him."
"18864","(18864) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: When he turned away, four months had passed. She broke up with him by divorcing him."
"18865","(18865) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Omar, and Ibn Abbas. They said: If he divorces and does not fulfill his duty until the four months have passed, then it is an irrevocable divorce."
"18866","(18866) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib, who said: I asked Saeed, the Emir of Mecca, about the Ila’a? He said: Ibn Abbas used to say: When four months had passed, she took control of her affairs, and Ibn Umar used to say that."
"18867","(18867) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The intention of divorce is extinguished. The four months, and the last is intercourse. (Bayhaqi 379)"
"18868","(18868) Hafs and Yazid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his commanders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ali, who said: When she passes Four months is an irrevocable divorce."
"18869","(18869) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Qubaysah, who said: When four months have passed, An irrevocable divorce."
"18870","(18870) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas (h) and on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, They said: If four months have passed, then your divorce is irrevocable."
"18871","(18871) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When four months have passed, An irrevocable divorce, and she has a divorce on her own."
"18872","(18872) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, who said: When four months had passed in the conquest, It was an irrevocable divorce, so I told Shurayh about a stolen statement, and he said so."
"18873","(18873) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin, who said: When four days have passed The months are an irrevocable divorce."
"18874","(18874) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Al-Musayyab, and Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman bin al-Harith bin Hisham, they said: If four months have passed since the end of the marriage, then he will be divorced, and this is more deserving. I brought her back."
"18875","(۱۸۸۷۵) حَدَّثَنَا ابْنُ مَہْدِیٍّ ، عَنْ سُفْیَانَ ، عَنْ إسْمَاعِیلَ بْنِ أُمَیَّۃَ ، عَنْ مَکْحُولٍ قَالَ : إذَا مَضَتْ أَرْبَعَۃُ There are only one month, and he has complete control over it."
"18876","(18876) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, who said: Ibn Anas had intercourse with his wife. She remained for six months, and while he was sitting in the gathering, he mentioned something, and Ibn Masoud came and said: Inform her that she has She took control of her affairs, so he came to her and told her, and she said: I will marry you, and he will give her a pound in charity."
"18877","(18877) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir, who said: I read in Abu Qalabi’s book with Ayyub: I asked Abu Salamah,"
"18878","(18878) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Ata’, who said: When four months have passed It is an irrevocable divorce, and her husband proposes to her during her waiting period, and no one else proposes to her."
"18879","(18879) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Amr bin Salma bin Harb; That Ali used to stop him after the four days until he made it clear whether he was going back or divorced."
"18880","(18880) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Bukair ibn Al-Akhnas, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Abi Laila; Ali stopped him."
"18881","(18881) Ibn Idris told us; On the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Marwan, on the authority of Ali, he said: He stops at the four until it indicates divorce, or taking him back."
"18882","(18882) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Marwan, on the authority of Ali, who said: As for me, I used to stop him after The four, either he will pay the ransom, or he will divorce, and Marwan said: If I had been appointed, I would have done the same as he does."
"18883","(18883) Ibn Aliyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Uthman; He used to say what the people of Medina said: it stops."
"18884","(18884) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar; Marwan stopped him after six months."
"18885","(18885) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar, on the authority of fifteen The Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He will stop."
"18886","(18886) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubair, who said: I asked Ibn Umar about the Ila’a? He said: The princes will decide on that."
"18887","(18887) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid (h) and on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, they said: In Al-Ilaa is stopped."
"18888","(18888) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul-Aziz; In the master: he stops."
"18889","(18889) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: It is not permissible for him to do anything but Whatever God commands him, he will either fulfill it or he will resolve it."
"18890","(18890) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hasan bin Furat, on the authority of Ibn Abi Maliki, who said: I heard Aisha say: It is waqf. The Lord"
"18891","(18891) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If a man has intercourse with his wife, he stops before the four days have passed. The months, and it will be said to him: Fear God, and either He will repay you, or you will divorce him with a divorce that will be known."
"18892","(18892) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, similarly."
"18893","(18893) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The master stops at the end of the four days. Then it is his wife, and if he does not fulfill it, then it is an irrevocable divorce."
"18894","(18894) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: If four months have passed, either Either he will return, or he will divorce."
"18895","(18895) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ka’b, who said: Al-I’la is not something, it is waqf."
"18896","(18896) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Hanzala, he said: I heard Al-Qasim bin Muhammad and he was asked about Al-Ila’? He said: He stops and the one who asks him is asked: Have you been divorced? He said: No, but if he calls the imam, he will either fulfill it or leave."
"18897","(18897) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majliz; He did not consider divorce a divorce."
"18898","(18898) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, who said: I asked Saeed bin Al-Musayyab about Al-Ilaa? He said: It is nothing."
"18899","(18899) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Aban al-Attar, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Darda’ He said: Deprivation is a disobedience, and his wife should not be forbidden to him."
"18900","(18900) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, who said: I read in Abu Qalababi’s letter with Ayyub: I asked Urwa Ibn Al-Zubayr and Saeed Ibn Al-Musayyab? They said: It is a sin, not a divorce."
"18901","(18901) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas (h) and on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, They said: If four months have passed since the divorce, then it is an irrevocable divorce, and she must observe the waiting period of three menstrual periods."
"18902","(18902) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Ali bin Badhimah, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: When four days have passed A few months, which is an irrevocable divorce, and after that she is waiting for three menstrual periods."
"18903","(18903) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad, who said: She should observe the waiting period after four months, the number of divorced women."
"18904","(18904) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, who said: If a man has intercourse with his wife and four months have passed. After that, she must wait for three months, if she does not menstruate."
"18905","(18905) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: If a man has intercourse with his wife and four months have passed, then Divorce her, and she will receive the waiting period."
"18906","(18906) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, who said: There is no waiting period on her."
"18907","(18907) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; In the case of a man who has had intercourse with his wife until four months have passed, how should she observe the waiting period? He said: Three recitations are required."
"18908","(18908) Ali bin Musahir told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Amir al-Ahwal, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: If he His wife for one month, or two months, or three months, unless the limit has been reached, then it is not an Ilaa."
"18909","(18909) Hafs told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If he swears an oath less than the four, it is not an oath of loyalty."
"18910","(18910) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Zaid, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr. They said: If he swears an oath other than the four, then it is not an oath."
"18911","(18911) Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Concerning a man who swore not to be close to his wife for three months, then he left her until four months had passed. He said: No. Loyalty"
"18912","(18912) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Bura, on the authority of Abdullah; That a man had sex with his wife ten times, and Abdullah had sexual intercourse with him."
"18913","(18913) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of al-Hasan and Muhammad, who said: If a man has sexual intercourse with his wife, then He left her until four months had passed. It was an irrevocable divorce."
"18914","(18914) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, who said: If a man says to his wife: By God, I will not approach you today, So he left her for four months, so it was a departure."
"18915","(18915) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he swears less than four times, then he is a pupil."
"18916","(18916) Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam; Concerning a man who swears that he will not be intimate with his wife for a month. He said: He is a servant."
"18917","(18917) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’athai, who said: A man from the neighborhood came to love, and his wife died. He said: So I asked Alqamah, Al-Aswad, and Masruq, and they said: If he succeeds with his tongue, then he has succeeded."
"18918","(18918) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man has intercourse with his wife and he prevents him from Intercourse is an illness, or work, or an excuse on his part, or one of them, and he bears witness to the fact that it is sufficient for that."
"18919","(18919) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, who said: If he returns with his tongue, then he returns."
"18920","(18920) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said regarding the servant: If he is sick, or He was traveling, or she was menstruating, he testified to her."
"18921","(18921) Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of al-Hasan and Ikrimah, who said: If he has an excuse He was excused, but he testified that he had returned to her, so that was for him."
"18922","(18922) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a man has intercourse with his wife So he testified that he had fulfilled it, so that was for him."
"18923","(18923) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The fa’i is the collective."
"18924","(18924) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The intention of divorce is extinguished. Four months, and the last is intercourse."
"18925","(18925) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi and Al-Hakam. They said: There is no harm except the congregation."
"18926","(18926) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm except intercourse."
"18927","(18927) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: There is no fay except intercourse."
"18928","(18928) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Al-Fay’ is the collective."
"18929","(18929) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ali bin Badhimah, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Al-Fay’ is the collective."
"18930","(18930) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali, Ibn Masoud, and Ibn Abbas They said: Fay is intercourse, and Ibn Masoud said: If there is an ailment to him such as old age, illness, or imprisonment, then there is a period between it. And between intercourse, his reward is that he fulfills his heart and tongue."
"18931","(18931) Abd al-Salam told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr that he asked him about a man who had intercourse with his wife, and he said: He gets from her what a man gets from his wife, except that he does not have intercourse with her, and if four months pass before he has intercourse with her He is an irrevocable divorcer."
"18932","(18932) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Al-Fay’ is the collective."
"18933","(18933) Ismail Ibn Aliyya narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say regarding the deliverance from the slaves: If Two months passed, and her husband did not fulfill her duty, so the divorce had occurred."
"18934","(18934) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, regarding those from his mothers who reverted to him, he said: Their affliction is Sharan."
"18935","(18935) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, who said: Giving a slave woman half of the responsibility of a free woman."
"18936","(18936) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, the same."
"18937","(18937) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak in Al-Hurr, when he left his mother, or divorced her. Her iddah is half the iddah of a free woman."
"18938","(18938) His youth narrated to us, he said: Shu’ba narrated to us, he said: I asked the arbiter about the one who is appointed guardian from the slave women, and he said: Abraham said: I counted it in two months, and I asked Hammad and he said the same thing."
"18939","(18939) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he divorced, then he divorced, or he divorced, then he voided the divorce. Dedication"
"18940","(18940) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: They are like the horse of Rahan, whichever of them was taken before. And if they fall together, they will be taken away."
"18941","(18941) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say something similar to what Al-Sha’biyyah said."
"18942","(18942) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi; Concerning a man who takes guardianship from his wife, then divorces him. He said: If four months have passed before she has had three menstrual periods, then It was clear"
"18943","(18943) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Divorce destroys separation."
"18944","(18944) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Divorce destroys separation."
"18945","(18945) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Divorce destroys separation, and he said: Ali: They are two of my horsemen."
"18946","(18946) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Murah, on the authority of Amr bin Murah, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah On the authority of Abdullah, he said: Loyalty is in contentment and anger."
"18947","(18947) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Harith bin Umairah, on the authority of Umm Atiyya, who said: Jubayr said: To his wife: “My brother’s son is with your son.” She said: “I cannot breastfeed two.” He said: “So he swore that he would not even come close to her.” He was weaned, he said: When he was weaned, he passed by the assembly, and the people said: It was good that you fed him. He said: Then Jubair said: I swore not Bring her closer until she is weaned. He said: Then the people said: This is Ilaa. Then Ali said to him: If you did that out of anger, then no. Your wife is permissible for you, otherwise she is your wife."
"18948","(18948) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of the one who narrated to him, on the authority of Ali, who said: Loyalty only occurs in anger."
"18949","(18949) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Yazid, who said: I asked Al-Hasan about the loyalty, and he said: The loyalty is only what it was. In anger, he said: I asked Ibn Sirin and he said: I do not know what this is? And he recited the verses of revelation."
"18950","(18950) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, about a man who swore not to come near His wife until she weans her boys. They said: When four months have passed, then the calamity has entered."
"18951","(18951) Omar bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, who said: Fulfillment is in contentment. And anger is the same."
"18952","(18952) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir bin Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: There is no loyalty except By oath"
"18953","(18953) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Devotion does not take place except with an oath to have intercourse."
"18954","(18954) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Abu Hurr, who said: I asked al-Hasan about a man who abandoned his wife for seven years. Asher said: The migration has been prolonged. I said: Will calamity come upon him? He said: Did he swear? I said: No. He said: No loyalty except with an oath."
"18955","(18955) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no oath unless he swears an oath."
"18956","(18956) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Every oath prohibits intercourse until four days have passed. The most famous month is Ilaa."
"18957","(18957) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr bin Haram, who said: Jabir bin Zaid was asked about a man. He abandoned his wife and four months passed and he said: She is not forbidden to him unless he swore by God that he would not touch her, nor He will reconcile with her, but if he swears an oath to do so and does not take it back until four months have passed, then it has ended, and he The gods"
"18958","(18958) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, who said: There is no loyalty unless he swears an oath."
"18959","(18959) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Safar, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Every oath is forbidden. All together, this is Ilaa."
"18960","(18960) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Every oath is forbidden. All together, this is Ilaa."
"18961","(18961) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: If the waiting period for Ila’ has expired and he is divorced, then he does not count it as a divorce. Something"
"18962","(18962) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When a man says to his wife, “And she will observe the waiting period for him” in the matter of consummation, Or divorce: He is divorced, then his divorce is permissible for her, so if he says: You are divorced after her waiting period has expired, then it is not With something, he divorces what he does not own."
"18963","(18963) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan. He was asked about releasing a slave from freedom, and he said: He waited for four days. More months"
"18964","(18964) Abu Issam told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The slave’s payment is half of the free person’s payment."
"18965","(18965) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Ali bin Bathimah, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: No. During her waiting period, he proposed to someone else, and when her waiting period ended, he and the people were equal."
"18966","(18966) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad, who said: He proposed to her during her waiting period, but he did not propose to her during her waiting period. Other than him"
"18967","(18967) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: They used to say, or they talked about the Ila’: So Four months passed and he divorced her irrevocably and he could propose to her during her waiting period if he wished. Ibn Aoun said: So I said to Muhammad Amer said: He will propose to her during her waiting period and no one else will propose to her. He said: Amer is right."
"18968","(18968) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughirah, that he heard Ash-Sha’bi narrate that he heard something stolen. He said: If it passes Four months, one of which is permanent, and her husband proposes to her during her waiting period, and no one else proposes to her."
"18969","(18969) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: She should not observe the waiting period for her husband if he wants to He may marry her, but she must wait for three days from the people."
"18970","(18970) Ismail Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan that he used to say: For a divorced woman three times and A pregnant woman, and the one who takes care of her, and she is a pregnant woman, is responsible for maintenance."
"18971","(18971) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawwi, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: For the three-divorced woman and the freed slave. And the divorced women and the cursed ones, and they are pregnant, and they are entitled to maintenance unless that is stipulated for the divorced women."
"18972","(18972) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, about a man who married a woman and her family had intercourse with him, so he swore that he would not Build it. Al-Zuhri said: There is no Ila’ except after entering."
"18973","(18973) Abu Asim narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If he turns away from it before he enters it, then he is not With a sign of loyalty, I said: Even if He has power over all of them? He said, even if He was able to bring them together."
"18974","(18974) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Abu Hashim, about a man who said to his wife: By God, no I live with my wife in this house, then he left her until four months had passed. He said: It is Ilaa, and Hammad said: Not with loyalty."
"18975","(18975) Waki` narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Mujahid, that Ibn al-Zubayr married A woman. They asked him for more in the dowry, so he swore that he would not do more or have intercourse with her until they were the ones seeking her. That is part of it. He said: So he left it for years, then they asked for it, so he entered with it, but he did not see it coming. Waki’ said: This is the saying. Sufyan and so we say."
"18976","(18976) Hafs bin Ghayath and Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Omar, who said: No. We permit the statement of a woman in the religion of God. A woman divorced three times is entitled to accommodation and maintenance. Ibn Fudail added: Aisha said: What It is better for her to remember this."
"18977","(18977) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Omar, and Abdullah, who said: She has the right to live and spend."
"18978","(18977) Hazrat Omar or Hazrat Abd Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"18979","(18979) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Ibrahim and Al-Shu’bi, who said: It is hers to live in and spend money on."
"18980","(18980) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: A divorced woman is entitled to maintenance as long as she is not in ihram. If she is forbidden, then she has the right to enjoy what is reasonable."
"18981","(18981) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, Ata’ and Al-Sha’abi. They said about a divorced woman three times: Laha. Residence and no expenses."
"18982","(18982) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: I mentioned to Ibrahim the hadith of Fatima bint Qais, and Ibrahim said: He said Omar: We do not abandon the Book of God and the Sunnah of His Messenger for the statement of a woman, we do not know, whether she has memorized it or forgotten, and Omar was making it for her. Residence and expenses."
"18983","(18983) Abdou bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, who said: I asked Saeed bin Al-Musayyab about a man who divorces His wife is in a rented house to whom? He said: On her husband. He said: If he is not with her husband. He said: On her. He said: If he is not with her? He said: Ali the prince."
"18984","(18984) Shabab told us, saying: Shu’ba told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: The divorced woman on the authority of three She has the right to live and spend money."
"18985","(18985) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Omar bin Al-Khattab said: We do not abandon the Book of our Lord and the Sunnah of our Prophet, according to the statement of the woman: The woman who is divorced three times is entitled to accommodation and maintenance."
"18986","(18986) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ja’far bin Burqan narrated to us, on the authority of Maimun bin Mihran, who said: Omar said: We will not abandon the Book of our Lord. And the Sunnah of our Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, according to the words of a woman."
"18987","(18987) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Mas’udi, on the authority of Al-Hikam, that a commentator said: A woman divorced for three times is entitled to accommodation and maintenance."
"18988","(18988) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Shu`ba narrated to us, on the authority of al-Hakam and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The woman who is divorced three times has the right to Residence and expenses."
"18989","(18989) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi al-Jahm bin Sakhir al-Adawi, who said: I heard Fatima bint Qays saying: Her husband divorced her three times, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not grant her a residence. And no spending. (Muslim 48. Tirmidhi 1135)"
"18990","(18990) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Fatima bint Qais said: My husband divorced me according to the covenant of the Messenger of God. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, three times. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: I will not provide you with residence or support.\n(Muslim 1117, Tirmidhi 1180)"
"18991","(18991) Fudayl bin Iyad narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A person who has been divorced three times is not forced to provide maintenance."
"18992","(18992) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, and Al-Hasan, who said: I heard them both say: The woman who is divorced three times. The deceased has neither residence nor maintenance."
"18993","(18993) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Ali bin Muslim, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, regarding the divorced woman. Three things we do not spend on."
"18994","(18994) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Ali bin Hakim, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: No. Spend on her"
"18995","(18995) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: I asked him about a man who divorces Is your wife absolutely free from any maintenance? He said: We do not spend on her."
"18996","(18996) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: He should not divorce her. She is pregnant, and God will pity her, and he will support her pregnancy and her breastfeeding until she is weaned."
"18997","(18997) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say: If a man divorces his wife three times, She is pregnant, and she is entitled to support, whether she is a free woman or a mother."
"18998","(18998) Hatim narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father; Concerning a man who divorces his wife absolutely, he said: We will not spend on her unless she is pregnant, and he will spend on her until she gives birth."
"18999","(18999) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The woman who is divorced three times and the one he takes care of her. And the divorced women and the cursed ones, while they are pregnant, are the ones who have to pay."
"19000","(19000) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Every pregnant woman has a maintenance allowance."
"19001","(19001) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Zakaria, who said: Amer was asked about a woman whose husband divorces her and... Should a pregnant woman spend on her? He said: Yes, if he is free."
"19002","(19002) Ibn Abi Ghani told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak: {So spend on them until they give birth} He said: If he divorces her while she is pregnant, he will spend on her until she gives birth."
"19003","(19003) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, that Abu al-Aaliyah and Shurayh said: In The pregnant woman with divorce: she is entitled to maintenance."
"19004","(19004) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: She is entitled to support unless he stipulates."
"19005","(19005) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: She has the right to provide for her, unless he stipulates that she should. He said and said: Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father: She has the right to spend, and Amr bin Dinar said: She has the right to spend, but he only spends on his children."
"19006","(19006) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Al-Qasim regarding the pregnant divorced woman: It is necessary to He spent"
"19007","(19007) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, who said: She is entitled to maintenance."
"19008","(19008) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: He used to provide for her if she was pregnant."
"19009","(19009) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: For every pregnant woman. He spent"
"19010","(19010) Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, that he said regarding the pregnant woman who has divorced: she has Tenderness"
"19011","(19011) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, Al-Hasan and Jabir bin Abdullah They said: We do not spend on her."
"19012","(19012) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; A free woman under a male slave and a female slave under a free woman are divorced while they are pregnant, and they are entitled to maintenance."
"19013","(19013) Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of al-Shaybani, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, regarding a slave who divorces his wife. And she is pregnant and said: She has to support herself until she gives birth."
"19014","(19014) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: If a slave divorces his wife while he is free, he will spend on her until she gives birth. If she gives birth, he does not spend on it."
"19015","(19015) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: If a free woman is married to a slave woman, then he divorces her. He has to support her until she gives birth, but he does not have to pay for breastfeeding."
"19016","(19016) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-Zubayr ibn Adiy, on the authority of Zayd ibn al-Harith, on the authority of Shurayh that a man He was divorced but did not part with him and did not consummate the marriage, so Shurayh forced him to be married."
"19017","(19017) Hafs ibn Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of the one who narrated to him, on the authority of Ibn Mughaffal, who said: He is only forced to divorce someone who is divorced and does not He assumed and did not enter."
"19018","(19018) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If a man divorces his wife and does not fulfill the obligation for her and does not He enters it and is forced to enjoy it."
"19019","(19019) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham, who said: The person who enjoys pleasure is only forced to He divorced but did not divorce and did not consummate marriage."
"19020","(19020) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, who said: He may give her pleasure for the equivalent of half a dowry."
"19021","(19021) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: If a man divorces his wife before He enters with her, and before he makes an allotment for her, she has nothing but possessions."
"19022","(19022) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, regarding someone who was divorced and did not separate before consummation. He said: Layha. Al-mut'i, and Ibn Sirin said: It has nothing to do with mut'i."
"19023","(19023) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Every divorced woman has a companion except the one who is divorced. She was divorced before he consummated the marriage with her, so she is entitled to half the dowry."
"19024","(19024) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: Every divorced person has his own marriage, whether he has entered into it, or he has not entered into it, an obligation. Layha, or he did not make it obligatory for her."
"19025","(19025) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far al-Razi, on the authority of al-Rabi`, on the authority of Abu al-Aliyah, who said: Every divorced woman has property."
"19026","(19026) Abd al-Razzaq told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: Every divorced woman has a companion."
"19027","(19027) Yazeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, who said: I said to Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab: Indeed, Al-Hasan and Aba Al-Aliyah is given to the divorced woman to whom the property was entered into and to the one to whom the property was not entered into. Sa’id said: It was only In Surah Al-Ahzab, when Surah Al-Baqarah was revealed, half of the dowry was imposed on her, and she was not entitled to any allowance for her."
"19028","(19028) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Every divorced woman has property except the woman. She was divorced and it was imposed on her."
"19029","(19029) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He was asked: A man divorces his wife and he has An obligation before he consummated the marriage with her. Does she have anything to do with her? He said: Ata used to say: There is no enjoyment for her."
"19030","(19030) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: If a man divorces a woman and he has prescribed for her, then she gets half the dowry. And no possessions for her."
"19031","(19031) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Mas’udi, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: She has The half is for belongings, meaning that which he did not enter with."
"19032","(19032) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Salih bin Ibrahim, that Abd al-Rahman bin Awf bathed His wife who divorced a black slave girl."
"19033","(19033) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, that he was informed that Anas bin Malik had pleasure with his wife for three hundred dirhams."
"19034","(19034) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Saad, on the authority of his father, that Al-Hasan bin Ali enjoyed His wife is worth ten thousand."
"19035","(19035) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Iyas, on the authority of Abu Majlaz, who said: I asked Ibn Umar about Al-Mu'ta'i said: He counted such-and-such, until he counted thirty."
"19036","(19036) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Shurayh that he divorced his wife, so he enjoyed three days with her. A hundred"
"19037","(19037) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad that he divorced his wife and enjoyed three hundred million."
"19038","(19038) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad that he enjoyed three hundred days of enjoyment."
